E["npc:deathwing"] = {t="npc",n="Deathwing",z="badlands",s="Deathwing the Destroyer, once known as Neltharion the Earth-Warder, is the fallen Dragon Aspect of the black dragonflight. Driven mad by the dark whispers of the Old Gods, he turned against the other Aspects and plunged the world into fire and turmoil. Though defeated near Grim Batol after the Second War and believed slain or hidden away, the terror of his legacy still haunts the deep places of Azeroth.",h="Deathwing the Destroyer, once known as Neltharion the Earth-Warder, is the fallen Dragon Aspect of the black...",sec={{t="The Fall of Neltharion",b="Before he was known as the Destroyer, Neltharion was granted dominion over the earth and the subterranean vaults of Azeroth by the titan pantheon. Yet dwelling so close to the world's deepest chambers exposed him to the insidious whispers of the imprisoned Old Gods. During the ancient War of the Ancients, the madness took complete hold. He deceived the other Dragon Aspects into imbuing a golden disc, the Dragon Soul, with portions of their essence under the guise of halting the Burning Legion, only to turn the terrible weapon against his allies and unleash catastrophic devastation.",sp=0},{t="Scheme of the Human Lord",b="Following the Second War, Deathwing sought to tear down mortal kingdoms from within. Taking the human identity of Lord Daval Prestor, a charismatic noble, he charmed King Terenas Menethil II and the high council of the Alliance of Lordaeron, plotting to install himself on the vacant throne of Alterac. Meanwhile, he aided the Dragonmaw clan at Grim Batol to keep Queen Alexstrasza enslaved while harvesting her clutches. His machinations unraveled when Rhonin destroyed the Demon Soul, restoring the other Aspects' stolen power and enabling them to drive Deathwing away.",sp=1},{t="The Brood Left Behind",b="In the present year, the mortal kingdoms largely assume Deathwing was destroyed or permanently driven from the world. However, the black dragonflight remains an active scourge across Azeroth. Led by his cunning brood, including his daughter Onyxia and son Nefarian, black drakes manipulate the politics of mortals and terrorize the landscape from mountain lairs. The scars of the black Aspect's ancient treachery run deep, and travelers wandering through craggy wastelands and deep subterranean tunnels still fear the stirring of the Great Dragon.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Deathwing originally?",a="Deathwing was originally Neltharion the Earth-Warder, the leader of the black dragonflight empowered by the titans to shepherd the land and mountains of Azeroth. Millennia ago, proximity to the deep earth made him vulnerable to the insidious whispers of the Old Gods, eroding his sanity.",al={"neltharion history","who is neltharion","earth warder origin"}},{q="What was the Dragon Soul?",a="The Dragon Soul, later known as the Demon Soul, was a golden artifact forged by Neltharion during the War of the Ancients. He tricked the other four Aspects into channeling their powers into it, then turned the weapon's apocalyptic force against his fellow dragons and mortal defenders alike.",al={"demon soul","what is the dragon soul","neltharion's artifact"}},{q="Who was Lord Daval Prestor?",a="Lord Daval Prestor was a human disguise adopted by Deathwing after the Second War. Through powerful charm magic and courtly deception, he attempted to claim the throne of Alterac and manipulate the Alliance of Lordaeron from within before his treachery was exposed.",al={"lord prestor","daval prestor identity","prestor lore"},sp=1},{q="What is Deathwing's connection to Grim Batol?",a="Deathwing covertly provided the Dragonmaw orcs with the Demon Soul at Grim Batol, ensuring the red dragon queen Alexstrasza remained chained and bred for war. Later, Rhonin destroyed the artifact with one of Deathwing's scales. Their powers restored, the other Aspects fought Deathwing and drove him away.",al={"deathwing grim batol","what happened at grim batol"}},{q="Who leads the black dragonflight today?",a="With Deathwing absent and presumed dead, his primary scions operate independently. His daughter Onyxia broods in her lair in Dustwallow Marsh, while his son Nefarian commands black dragons and experiments with dragonsblood high atop Blackrock Mountain.",al={"current black dragon leader","who leads black dragons","nefarian and onyxia"},sp=2}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The nobility of the Alliance still shudders at how close Lord Daval Prestor came to seizing the crown of Alterac and manipulating the Council of Seven Nations to destroy the Alliance from within.",["faction:Horde"]="The Old Horde made a wicked bargain with Deathwing during the Second War to secure red dragons via the Dragonmaw clan, a stain the new Horde seeks to leave in the past.",["race:NightElf"]="Kaldorei elders remember Neltharion's sudden, devastating betrayal ten thousand years ago during the War of the Ancients, an atrocity that broke dragonkind and sealed the doom of their ancient empire."},kw={"aspect","black dragonflight","deathwing","demon soul","destroyer","dragon soul","earth-warder","grim batol","neltharion","prestor"},rel={"topic:black-dragonflight","topic:war-of-the-ancients","subzone:grim-batol","topic:old-god","topic:alliance-of-lordaeron","topic:old-horde","topic:second-war"},src={"Deathwing"}}
E["npc:lotwil-veriatus"] = {t="npc",n="Lotwil Veriatus",z="badlands",s="Lotwil Veriatus is an eccentric gnomish scholar conducting dangerous elemental experiments in the dusty wastes of the Badlands. Stationed east of Kargath with his sarcastic apprentice Lucien Tosselwrench and a mechanical attendant named Servo, he is dedicated to blending arcane theory, alchemy, and engineering into a unified discipline.",h="Lotwil Veriatus is an eccentric gnomish scholar conducting dangerous elemental experiments in the dusty...",sec={{t="A Unified Field of Chaos",b="Originally from Kharanos in Dun Morogh, Lotwil envisions a grand University for his Enlightened Assembly of Arcanology, Alchemy, and Engineering Sciences. He believes these three disciplines should not be practiced in isolation, but harmonized. In pursuit of this dream, he chose the harsh Badlands as his laboratory to study native rock elementals and construct binding shackles capable of mastering elemental forces. While an accomplished researcher—having studied elemental machines and defeated dark iron constructs in the past—his single-minded focus often blinds him to the explosive hazards of his fieldwork.",sp=0},{t="The Elemental Shackles",b="Lotwil's grand ambition in the Badlands centers on testing his shackles of elemental binding. By tasking adventurers with collecting rock elemental cores, coolant, and gyrochronatoms, he prepares an elaborate ritual intended to subjugate an elemental servant. However, when the binding device is finally activated, the convergence of volatile magic, erratic engineering, and unstable alchemical reagents goes catastrophically awry, conjuring a towering, enraged elemental monstrosity named Fam'retor that turns on its creator.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Lotwil Veriatus?",a="Lotwil Veriatus is a gnomish savant residing in an isolated camp east of Kargath in the Badlands. He is a founding member of the Enlightened Assembly of Arcanology, Alchemy, and Engineering Sciences, seeking to blend all three fields into a single academic discipline.",al={"who is lotwil","lotwil veriatus lore","gnome in badlands"}},{q="Why is Lotwil out in the Badlands?",a="Lotwil came to the Badlands to study the region's dense concentration of wild rock elementals. The open desert offers both raw elemental material and enough space to conduct volatile binding experiments without endangering major population centers.",al={"why is lotwil in badlands","lotwil badlands camp","what is lotwil doing"}},{q="Who is Lucien Tosselwrench?",a="Lucien Tosselwrench is Lotwil's long-suffering gnomish assistant. Thoroughly cynical and exhausted by his master's eccentric ramblings, Lucien manages logistics, repairs the mechanical servant Servo, and routinely warns bystanders about Lotwil's dangerous carelessness.",al={"lucien tosselwrench","lotwil assistant","lotwil apprentice"}},{q="What happens when Lotwil finishes his experiment?",a="Lotwil attempts to use his custom-crafted shackles of elemental binding to enslave an elemental construct. The hybrid technology fails spectacularly, summoning an enormous, enraged rock elemental named Fam'retor that must be slain before it destroys his camp.",al={"lotwil experiment fail","shackles of elemental binding","fam'retor"},sp=1}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Lotwil exemplifies gnomish intellectual ambition taken to reckless extremes, seeking to bridge engineering and the arcane regardless of the catastrophic risks.",["profession:Engineering"]="Engineers will recognize Lotwil's ambition to integrate mechanical gyros and gears into arcane containment fields, as well as the classic engineering pitfall of sudden, violent malfunction."},kw={"badlands","elemental","fam'retor","kargath","lotwil","lucien","servo","veriatus"},rel={"zone:badlands","subzone:kargath","subzone:kharanos","topic:gnome","topic:goblin","topic:third-war"},src={"Lotwil Veriatus"}}
E["npc:prospector-ryedol"] = {t="npc",n="Prospector Ryedol",z="badlands",s="Prospector Ryedol is an Explorers' League surveyor stationed on a dusty rise overlooking the eastern Badlands. Watching over the perilous excavations below, he strives to recover lost dwarven relics and maintain hope in a barren wasteland overrun by troggs and beasts.",h="Prospector Ryedol is an Explorers' League surveyor stationed on a dusty rise overlooking the eastern Badlands.",sec={{t="Watching Over the Digs",b="Perched upon a rugged hill just south of Hammertoe's Digsite, Prospector Ryedol represents the ongoing efforts of Ironforge's Explorers' League in the Badlands. The arid valley is rich in ancient titan secrets and earthen heritage, but field expeditions here are constantly beleaguered by savage troggs, ravenous coyotes, and territorial drakes. Ryedol coordinates retrieval efforts for dwarven gear stolen by the Dark Iron dwarves and seeks signs of hope amid the ruined outposts, determined not to let the League's sacrifices in the wastes be in vain.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Prospector Ryedol?",a="Ryedol is a dwarven field researcher for the Explorers' League. He has made his camp on a high hill overlooking Hammertoe's Digsite in the eastern Badlands, where he helps direct salvage and recovery missions.",al={"ryedol","who is ryedol","prospector ryedol location"}},{q="What is Ryedol doing in the Badlands?",a="He is stationed in the Badlands to support the Explorers' League's archaeological ventures. With several nearby digsites compromised or overrun by Dark Iron dwarves and troggs, he works with travelers to secure recovered relics, track lost tools, and verify the fate of his fellow dwarves.",al={"what is ryedol doing","ryedol's mission","why is ryedol here"}},{q="What is Ryedol's Hammer?",a="Ryedol's Hammer is a reward for recovering his Lucky Pick from the Dark Iron dwarves who attacked Hammertoe's Digsite. The stolen item is his pick, not the reward hammer.",al={"ryedol hammer","dwarf and his tools"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Ryedol represents Ironforge's unyielding drive to uncover the origins of the dwarven race, even when digging in the harshest reaches of Khaz Modan.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance adventurers traversing the dangerous wastes of the Badlands, Ryedol provides a friendly face and an urgent set of tasks in support of the Explorers' League."},kw={"badlands","digsite","explorers' league","hammertoe","ironforge","prospector ryedol","ryedol"},rel={"zone:badlands","topic:explorers-league","topic:dwarf"},src={"Prospector Ryedol"}}
E["npc:theldurin-the-lost"] = {t="npc",n="Theldurin the Lost",z="badlands",s="Theldurin the Lost is a reclusive, half-mad dwarf wandering the scorched expanses of the Badlands. Formerly aligned with the insidious Twilight's Hammer cult, he fled their ranks with stolen sacred relics after realizing the horror of their designs.",h="Theldurin the Lost is a reclusive, half-mad dwarf wandering the scorched expanses of the Badlands.",sec={{t="A Mind Fractured by Darkness",b="Perched in the barren hills of the Badlands, clutching bags of explosives in wild paranoia, Theldurin is far more than a simple mad hermit. He was once an initiate of the Twilight's Hammer cult. When the sinister cabal sought to awaken a primordial elemental power trapped beneath the earth, Theldurin recoiled in terror, rejected their mad teachings, and fled into the desert. He carried with him the Scroll of Myzrael, desperate to prevent his former masters from unleashing an ancient horror upon the world. Though the escape cost him his sanity, his defiance dealt a serious blow to the cult's plans.",sp=0},{t="A Desperate Countermeasure",b="Survival in the wastes proved bitter. Enraged earth elementals ambushed Theldurin and tore his stolen scroll to pieces, scattering the fragments across the dust. Now besieged by paranoia and haunted by visions of an impending doom slumbering beneath the surface, the crazed dwarf seeks ancient texts—the Tablet of Ryun'eh and Yagyin's Digest—hoping to uncover long-buried lore. Rather than allow the cult to free the elemental princess Myzrael at the height of her fury, Theldurin plots to force her premature summoning so she can be defeated and bound once again.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Theldurin the Lost?",a="Theldurin is a mad dwarven hermit hiding in the Badlands. He is a former member of the Twilight's Hammer cult who stole their ritual secrets and fled into the wilderness to stop them from unleashing a dangerous power.",al={"who is theldurin","theldurin lore","mad dwarf badlands"}},{q="Why is Theldurin hiding in the Badlands?",a="He is on the run from the Twilight's Hammer. After stealing the Scroll of Myzrael from the cult, he took refuge in the remote, sun-baked canyons of the Badlands to stay ahead of the cultists hunting him down.",al={"why is theldurin here","why does theldurin hide","theldurin badlands"}},{q="What is the Scroll of Myzrael?",a="It is an arcane parchment holding the ritual knowledge required to release Myzrael, an ancient, corrupted elemental entity trapped deep beneath Arathi. Theldurin stole it so the Twilight's Hammer could not complete their summoning, though local elementals later shredded the document into pieces.",al={"scroll of myzrael","what scroll did theldurin steal"},sp=1},{q="What does Theldurin want to do with Myzrael?",a="Knowing the bindings on the creature are weakening, Theldurin seeks to summon Myzrael prematurely before she gathers her full strength. By forcing her forth weakened, adventurers can banish and re-seal her beneath the crust before the Twilight's Hammer can master her power.",al={"theldurin plan","why summon myzrael","summoning the princess"},sp=1}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Seeing a fellow son of Ironforge reduced to raving paranoia in a wasteland is tragic, but his refusal to bow to dark cults reveals enduring dwarven stubbornness.",["profession:Engineering"]="Theldurin threatens approaching strangers with a pack brimming with blastpowder, exhibiting an unpredictable reliance on volatile explosives."},kw={"badlands","blastpowder","myzrael","ryun'eh","scroll of myzrael","theldurin","theldurin the lost","twilight's hammer"},rel={"topic:twilight-s-hammer","zone:badlands","topic:dwarf","topic:old-god","zone:ironforge","zone:undercity"},src={"Theldurin the Lost"}}
E["npc:warlord-goretooth"] = {t="npc",n="Warlord Goretooth",z="badlands",s="Warlord Goretooth is the commanding orc officer stationed at Kargath in the dusty wastes of the Badlands. From his watchtower, he coordinates the Horde's frontier campaigns against the neighboring Dark Iron dwarves and monitors the volcanic menace of Blackrock Mountain. Though strict in military matters, he can occasionally be found relaxing around the camp's bonfire.",h="Warlord Goretooth is the commanding orc officer stationed at Kargath in the dusty wastes of the Badlands.",sec={{t="Commander of Kargath",b="Perched atop the watchtower of Kargath, Warlord Lunk Goretooth directs Horde operations on the hostile eastern frontier. Kargath serves as Orgrimmar's primary staging ground against the threats lurking within Blackrock Mountain and the surrounding ravines. Goretooth oversees patrols, coordinates scout forces like the Kargath Expeditionary Force, and issues direct kill orders targeting the Dark Iron clan's ranks and leadership. When he descends from his lookout, the stern commander shows a lighter side, frequently warming himself by the camp bonfire and trading quips with the camp's Forsaken casters before returning to duty.",sp=0},{t="Striking the Dark Irons",b="Goretooth views the Dark Iron dwarves as a clear and present threat to Horde interests in the Eastern Kingdoms. Rather than engaging in defensive posturing, he pursues aggressive war plans against General Angerforge and Emperor Dagran Thaurissan's forces entrenched within Blackrock Depths. Recognizing the gravity of assaulting such an ancient subterranean stronghold, he frequently defers strategic matters to veteran orcs like Eitrigg in Orgrimmar, seeking seasoned wisdom before sanctioning further pushes into the mountain.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Warlord Goretooth?",a="Warlord Goretooth is the senior Horde military commander stationed at Kargath in the Badlands. He organizes Horde patrols and directs incursions against the Dark Iron dwarves.",al={"warlord goretooth","who is goretooth","goretooth badlands","kargath commander"}},{q="What is his role in Kargath?",a="He commands the outpost, regularly dispatches the Kargath Expeditionary Force into the field, and issues military orders for operations against the Dark Iron clan inside Blackrock Depths.",al={"what does goretooth do","goretooth duties","goretooth post"}},{q="Why is Goretooth sending soldiers against Blackrock Depths?",a="The Dark Iron dwarves threaten the surrounding regions and actively oppose Horde presence in the area. Goretooth issues direct kill bounties against their soldiers, high-ranking officers, and General Angerforge to weaken their hold on the mountain.",al={"why kill dark irons","death to angerforge quest","goretooth dark iron"}},{q="Why does Goretooth consult Eitrigg?",a="Eitrigg is a seasoned orc veteran who lived inside Blackrock Mountain and understands its internal politics and defenses better than almost anyone. Goretooth sends adventurers to seek Eitrigg's counsel before escalating assaults on Blackrock strongholds.",al={"goretooth and eitrigg","eitriggs wisdom","why talk to eitrigg"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Warlord Goretooth is the cornerstone of the Horde's foothold in the Badlands, directing critical operations against the Dark Iron dwarves.",["class:Warrior"]="Goretooth's brutal, straightforward military orders in Blackrock Mountain offer martial champions a chance to test their mettle against seasoned dwarven legionnaires."},kw={"angerforge","badlands","blackrock","dark iron","eitrigg","goretooth","kargath","warlord goretooth"},rel={"subzone:kargath","zone:badlands","npc:eitrigg","topic:horde"},src={"Warlord Goretooth"}}
E["quest:1419"] = {t="quest",n="Coyote Thieves",z="badlands",s="In the outpost of Kargath, Neeka Bloodscar wants you to hunt the crag coyotes of the Badlands, tough beasts that have dared to sneak into Kargath and steal its food. Thirty jawbones are what Neeka asks for.",h="In the outpost of Kargath, Neeka Bloodscar wants you to hunt the crag coyotes of the Badlands, tough beasts...",sec={{t="Thieves of Kargath",b="Neeka Bloodscar asks whether you have spent many days in the Badlands, felt its heat and met the beasts of its dusty plains. Crag coyotes are a tough breed, and they have crept into Kargath to steal from the outpost's food. Neeka wants them hunted and their jawbones brought back. Bring enough, and Neeka may believe you know the Badlands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Neeka Bloodscar want coyote jawbones?",a="Crag coyotes have sneaked into Kargath and stolen from its food supplies. Neeka wants them hunted, and wants jawbones as proof that you know the Badlands.",al={"why coyote jawbones","neeka bloodscar motivation","why collect jawbones"}},{q="Where are the coyotes causing trouble?",a="Crag coyotes wander the dusty plains of the Badlands, and they have crept into the outpost of Kargath to steal food.",al={"coyote location","where to find crag coyotes","where are the coyotes"}},{q="How many jawbones does Neeka Bloodscar want?",a="Thirty coyote jawbones, brought to Neeka Bloodscar in Kargath.",al={"how many jawbones","coyote jawbone count"}},{q="Who is Neeka Bloodscar?",a="Neeka Bloodscar is at the outpost of Kargath in the Badlands, where Neeka gives out this hunt.",al={"who is neeka","neeka bloodscar"}}},kw={"badlands","coyote thieves","crag coyote","jawbones","kargath","neeka bloodscar"},rel={"subzone:kargath","zone:badlands"},m={start="Neeka Bloodscar",["end"]="Neeka Bloodscar",level="40",faction="Horde",id=1419},src={"Coyote Thieves"}}
E["quest:1420"] = {t="quest",n="Report to Helgrum",z="badlands",s="Neeka Bloodscar has written a fresh report for Helgrum the Swift in Stonard, and asks you to carry it there. This follows your visit to Neeka at Kargath.",h="Neeka Bloodscar has written a fresh report for Helgrum the Swift in Stonard, and asks you to carry it there.",sec={{t="A Report for Stonard",b="Neeka Bloodscar has written a new report for Helgrum in Stonard and hands it to you. Neeka adds that anyone who calls themselves an outrunner must not lose the way, or fall to an enemy.",sp=0},{t="Helgrum Reads the Report",b="Reading Neeka's report, Helgrum sees that the Alliance has troubles of its own. Helgrum also thinks the Horde and the Alliance may turn out to share some enemies.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you with the report?",a="Neeka Bloodscar, who has written a fresh report for Helgrum.",al={"who gives report to helgrum","quest giver report to helgrum","who starts this quest"}},{q="Where does the report need to be delivered?",a="To Helgrum the Swift in Stonard.",al={"where to turn in report to helgrum","helgrum location","where is helgrum"}},{q="What comes before this?",a="It follows the earlier step in which Helgrum sent you to speak with Neeka Bloodscar at Kargath.",al={"previous quest","prerequisite for report to helgrum","what quest comes first"}}},kw={"badlands","helgrum the swift","horde intelligence","neeka bloodscar","outrunner","report","stonard"},rel={"quest:1418","subzone:stonard","zone:badlands","topic:alliance"},m={start="Neeka Bloodscar",["end"]="Helgrum the Swift",level="40",faction="Horde",id=1420},src={"Report to Helgrum"}}
E["quest:2258"] = {t="quest",n="Badlands Reagent Run",z="badlands",s="In the outpost of Kargath, Jarkal Mossmeld, an alchemist of some note, needs reagents found out in the Badlands to replenish stocks. Coin is promised, but only to someone who brings the goods.",h="In the outpost of Kargath, Jarkal Mossmeld, an alchemist of some note, needs reagents found out in the...",sec={{t="Stocking the Shelves",b="Jarkal Mossmeld is short on ingredients: gizzards from five buzzards, fangs from ten crag coyotes, and shards from five rock elementals. All three can be taken from the creatures themselves. Anyone who is not the fighting type is told to find friends who are. Jarkal pays in coin, but only once the reagents are in hand.",sp=0},{t="After the Haul",b="Pleased with the haul, Jarkal says it should last a little while. The alchemist has more reagents to gather, but these can be found only far down inside the Uldaman excavation and will not be easy to get. Jarkal hints that the pay may be worth more than shiny coins.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is asking for these reagents?",a="Jarkal Mossmeld, an alchemist of some note at the outpost of Kargath in the Badlands, who wants to replenish the stocks.",al={"who gives badlands reagent run","jarkal mossmeld","who is jarkal mossmeld"}},{q="What ingredients does Jarkal need?",a="Gizzards from five buzzards, fangs from ten crag coyotes and shards from five rock elementals. All of them come from the creatures themselves.",al={"what items needed","badlands reagents list","reagents required"}},{q="Where is Jarkal Mossmeld located?",a="Jarkal is in the outpost of Kargath, in the Badlands.",al={"jarkal mossmeld location","where is kargath alchemist","where to turn in badlands reagent run"}},{q="What does Jarkal offer in exchange for the ingredients?",a="Coin, paid once the reagents are brought to Jarkal in Kargath. Nothing is paid before then.",al={"badlands reagent run reward","what do i get"}}},kw={"alchemy","badlands","buzzard gizzard","crag coyote fang","jarkal mossmeld","kargath","rock elemental shard","uldaman"},rel={"subzone:kargath","zone:badlands","subzone:uldaman"},m={start="Jarkal Mossmeld",["end"]="Jarkal Mossmeld",level="39",faction="Horde",id=2258},src={"Badlands Reagent Run (Horde)"}}
E["quest:3821"] = {t="quest",n="Dreadmaul Rock",z="badlands",s="Thal'trak Proudtusk's wife Sha'ni was sent over three weeks ago to look into strange rituals among the Firegut ogres, and nobody has heard from her platoon. Thal'trak cannot leave his post, so he asks you to go and learn what became of her.",h="Thal'trak Proudtusk's wife Sha'ni was sent over three weeks ago to look into strange rituals among the...",sec={{t="A Husband Without Word",b="Sha'ni's orders took her to the Burning Steppes, to look into strange rituals among the Firegut ogres. That was more than three weeks ago. Goretooth says nothing has been heard from anyone in her platoon, and advises Thal'trak to put it behind him and keep to his duty. Thal'trak will not accept that, for it is his wife who is missing. He cannot leave his post, so he asks you to go there and search for her.",sp=0},{t="Sha'ni's Words",b="Sha'ni speaks of Thal'trak with pity. The two had planned to move in with her mother and father in the Hinterlands once their tours were over, and now those plans are ruined.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Thal'trak looking for?",a="His wife, Sha'ni Proudtusk, who was sent into the Burning Steppes to look into strange rituals among the Firegut ogres and has not been heard from.",al={"who is missing","thaltrak wife","sha'ni proudtusk"}},{q="Why did Sha'ni go to the Burning Steppes?",a="She was sent there more than three weeks ago to look into reports of strange rituals among the Firegut ogres.",al={"shani mission","firegut ogre ritual","why did shani leave"}},{q="Why hasn't Thal'trak searched for her himself?",a="He cannot leave his post, so he asks you to go in his place.",al={"why cant thaltrak go","why is thaltrak waiting"}},{q="What does Goretooth say about the missing platoon?",a="Goretooth has heard nothing from anyone in that platoon, and tells Thal'trak to put it behind him and keep to his duty.",al={"goretooth response","what does goretooth say"}}},kw={"badlands","burning steppes","dreadmaul rock","firegut ogres","goretooth","sha'ni proudtusk","thal'trak proudtusk"},rel={"zone:burningsteppes","subzone:dreadmaul-rock","zone:badlands","zone:hinterlands"},m={start="Thal'trak Proudtusk",["end"]="Sha'ni Proudtusk",level="52",faction="Horde",id=3821},src={"Dreadmaul Rock (quest)"}}
E["quest:4062"] = {t="quest",n="The Rise of the Machines",z="badlands",s="Hierophant Theodora Mulvadania has found initials and a rank marking on the elemental shards, and the machines you brought down in the Burning Steppes bore Rank IV. Theodora sends you with a shard sample to Lotwil Veriatus, a scholar of elemental sciences, in a camp to the east.",h="Hierophant Theodora Mulvadania has found initials and a rank marking on the elemental shards, and the...",sec={{t="Marks on the Shards",b="The shards carry the initials G.L.A., with a rank marking beneath them. The machines you brought down in the Burning Steppes bore Rank IV, which Theodora assumes is a lowly rank. Theodora wants you to bring a sample shard to Lotwil Veriatus, renowned among scholars of elemental sciences. Lotwil is stationed at a camp to the east, and Theodora hopes Lotwil can help the search.",sp=0},{t="What Lotwil Sees",b="When you show Lotwil the shard, his face turns white. He knows these markings.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to Lotwil Veriatus?",a="Hierophant Theodora Mulvadania, who wants Lotwil to look at a sample shard from the machines destroyed in the Burning Steppes.",al={"who gives this quest","quest giver","theodora mulvadania"}},{q="Where is Lotwil Veriatus located?",a="In a camp to the east.",al={"where is lotwil","lotwil location","lotwil veriatus camp"}},{q="What markings are on the elemental shards?",a="The shards bear the initials G.L.A., with a rank marking below. The destroyed machines were of Rank IV.",al={"shard initials","what does gla mean","rank iv"}},{q="Why does Theodora want Lotwil to inspect the shard?",a="Lotwil is renowned among scholars of elemental sciences, and Theodora hopes he can help with the search.",al={"why lotwil","why consult lotwil"}}},kw={"badlands","burning steppes","elemental shard sample","g.l.a.","lotwil veriatus","rise of the machines","theodora mulvadania"},rel={"npc:lotwil-veriatus","zone:badlands","zone:burningsteppes"},m={start="Hierophant Theodora Mulvadania",["end"]="Lotwil Veriatus",level="54",faction="Horde",id=4062},src={"The Rise of the Machines (2)"}}
E["quest:692"] = {t="quest",n="The Lost Fragments",z="badlands",s="Theldurin the Lost is in a panic over the Scroll of Myzrael. Its magic could drag Myzrael up to the surface, yet if she is already free, the scroll may be the only way to bind her again. Elementals in a rage have shredded it and fight over the scraps, and you are sent to gather them.",h="Theldurin the Lost is in a panic over the Scroll of Myzrael.",sec={{t="A Dangerous Parchment",b="Theldurin the Lost is alarmed at the mention of the Scroll of Myzrael, fearing its magic could draw Myzrael to the surface. Then comes a change of heart: if she has already slipped free, or is gathering strength to strike, the scroll is just what you will need to trap her again.",sp=0},{t="Torn by the Elements",b="The scroll is no longer whole. Furious elementals took it, ripped it to shreds and now fight over the scraps. You are after three pieces, one torn, one crumpled and one singed, and Theldurin means to try mending them. The thieves roam the hills behind Theldurin.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you to collect the scroll fragments?",a="Theldurin the Lost asks you to bring back the pieces of the destroyed scroll.",al={"quest giver","who starts the lost fragments","theldurin quest"}},{q="What is the Scroll of Myzrael supposed to do?",a="Theldurin says its magic could draw Myzrael up to the surface. Theldurin also thinks that, if she is already free, it is what you would need to trap her again.",al={"what does the scroll do","scroll of myzrael lore","why find scroll fragments"}},{q="Where are the scroll fragments?",a="Elementals in a rage carried off the scroll, tore it up and fight over the pieces. They are in the hills behind Theldurin.",al={"who has the fragments","where to find the scroll pieces","scroll fragment location"}},{q="What comes before this quest?",a="It follows your earlier dealings with Theldurin the Lost.",al={"previous quest","prerequisite for the lost fragments"}}},kw={"badlands","crumpled scroll fragment","elementals","myzrael","scroll of myzrael","singed scroll fragment","theldurin the lost","torn scroll fragment"},rel={"npc:theldurin-the-lost","quest:687","quest:656","zone:badlands"},m={start="Theldurin the Lost",["end"]="Theldurin the Lost",level="41",id=692},src={"The Lost Fragments"}}
E["quest:703"] = {t="quest",n="Barbecued Buzzard Wings",z="badlands",s="Rigglefuzz swears by barbecued buzzard wings, a rich sauce on tangy meat. Everything for a batch is on hand except the wings themselves. Fetch enough of them and Rigglefuzz may part with the recipe.",h="Rigglefuzz swears by barbecued buzzard wings, a rich sauce on tangy meat.",sec={{t="A Local Favorite",b="Rigglefuzz is proud of barbecued buzzard wings. The sauce is rich, the meat tangy, and the aroma carries to hungry folk a long way off. Every ingredient for a batch is already in hand, all but the wings. Bring four buzzard wings, and Rigglefuzz might share the recipe.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who asks for the buzzard wings?",a="Rigglefuzz wants buzzard wings to cook a batch of barbecued buzzard wings.",al={"who gives barbecued buzzard wings","who is rigglefuzz","quest giver"}},{q="What does Rigglefuzz offer in return for the wings?",a="Rigglefuzz hints at sharing the recipe if you bring enough wings.",al={"what is the reward","what do i get","recipe reward"}},{q="Why does Rigglefuzz need buzzard wings?",a="Rigglefuzz has everything else needed for a batch of barbecued buzzard wings, and only the wings are missing.",al={"why buzzards","rigglefuzz motive","why does rigglefuzz want wings"}},{q="How many wings does Rigglefuzz want?",a="Four buzzard wings.",al={"how many buzzard wings","buzzard wing count"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Cooks take note: the recipe for the dish is on offer."},kw={"badlands","barbecue","buzzard","cooking","recipe","rigglefuzz","wings"},rel={"zone:badlands"},m={start="Rigglefuzz",["end"]="Rigglefuzz",level="40",id=703},src={"Barbecued Buzzard Wings"}}
E["quest:705"] = {t="quest",n="Pearl Diving",z="badlands",s="Rigglefuzz, a goblin, finds the Badlands full of vicious predators and bold scavengers, and survives by being tricky: flash bombs scare off the wildlife. The supply of crushed blue pearl powder is running low, so you are sent to the Vile Reef in Stranglethorn for more.",h="Rigglefuzz, a goblin, finds the Badlands full of vicious predators and bold scavengers, and survives by being...",sec={{t="A Tricky Little Goblin",b="The Badlands are harsh, and Rigglefuzz admits to being scared as a short little goblin among predators and scavengers. Rigglefuzz knows the recipe for flash bombs and uses them to frighten wildlife away. One ingredient is running low: crushed blue pearl powder.",sp=0},{t="Pearls from the Reef",b="Blue pearls come from the clams at the Vile Reef in Stranglethorn. Rigglefuzz jokes that you had better wear good boots, then waits in the Badlands for nine of them, promising to make your effort worthwhile.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Rigglefuzz need blue pearls?",a="Rigglefuzz uses crushed blue pearl powder to make flash bombs, and the supply is running low.",al={"rigglefuzz pearls","why pearl diving","why blue pearls"}},{q="Where are the blue pearls found?",a="They are found in clams at the Vile Reef in Stranglethorn.",al={"where are blue pearls","blue pearl location","vile reef pearls"}},{q="Why does Rigglefuzz use flash bombs?",a="The Badlands are full of vicious predators and bold scavengers, and flash bombs scare the wildlife away.",al={"why flash bombs","rigglefuzz defense"}},{q="How many blue pearls does Rigglefuzz want?",a="Nine blue pearls, brought back to Rigglefuzz in the Badlands.",al={"blue pearl count","how many pearls"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Engineers have good reason to take an interest in Rigglefuzz's flash bombs."},kw={"badlands","blue pearl","flash bomb","pearl diving","rigglefuzz","stranglethorn vale","vile reef"},rel={"zone:badlands","subzone:vile-reef","zone:stranglethorn","topic:goblin"},m={start="Rigglefuzz",["end"]="Rigglefuzz",level="37",id=705},src={"Pearl Diving"}}
E["quest:706"] = {t="quest",n="Fiery Blaze Enchantments",z="badlands",s="Sigrun Ironhew, waiting in the Badlands for word from Ironforge, knows a technique for imbuing weapons with fire. It needs blood from the still-beating heart of a rare black drake whelp, and the whelps of Lethlor Ravine are where to find one.",h="Sigrun Ironhew, waiting in the Badlands for word from Ironforge, knows a technique for imbuing weapons with...",sec={{t="An Apprentice's Craft",b="Sigrun Ironhew learned a special way of imbuing weapons with fiery enchantments as an apprentice to Feranor Steeltoe, last heard of among a hunting party's smiths in Lordaeron. Sigrun is waiting for word from Ironforge and has little else to do.",sp=0},{t="The Whelps of Lethlor Ravine",b="Sigrun will share few details of the process, only that it calls for blood from the still-beating heart of a rare black drake whelp. Take a heart from the whelps of that ravine to Sigrun and the skill will be shown to you. The Scalding Whelps and Scorched Guardians there are where the hearts come from.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who taught Sigrun Ironhew this enchantment technique?",a="Sigrun learned it as an apprentice to Feranor Steeltoe, last heard of in Lordaeron, with a hunting party's smithy.",al={"sigrun teacher","who trained sigrun","feranor steeltoe"}},{q="What component is needed to place fire upon a blade?",a="Blood drawn from the heart of a rare black drake whelp, one that still beats.",al={"what does sigrun need","black drake heart requirement","fiery blaze materials"}},{q="Where are the black drake whelps found?",a="In Lethlor Ravine, in the eastern Badlands.",al={"where to find black drakes","lethlor ravine whelps","black drake heart location"}},{q="Why is Sigrun Ironhew lingering in the Badlands?",a="Word from Ironforge is what Sigrun is waiting on, and nothing else is keeping Sigrun busy in the meantime.",al={"why is sigrun in badlands","sigrun ironhew purpose"}},{q="Which creatures yield the needed heart?",a="The Scalding Whelps and Scorched Guardians of Lethlor Ravine.",al={"what drops black drakes heart","which whelps have hearts"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Sigrun Ironhew looks to Ironforge for word, and this work is meant for the Alliance."},kw={"badlands","black drake heart","feranor steeltoe","fiery blaze","ironforge","lethlor ravine","scalding whelp","scorched guardian","sigrun ironhew"},rel={"subzone:lethlor-ravine","zone:badlands","zone:ironforge","topic:lordaeron"},m={start="Sigrun Ironhew",["end"]="Sigrun Ironhew",level="45",faction="Alliance",id=706},src={"Fiery Blaze Enchantments"}}
E["quest:708"] = {t="quest",n="The Black Box",z="badlands",s="A metallic black box has turned up in a giant condor's stomach in the Badlands, its surface heavily pitted as if left in acid. Stamped on its underside, beneath a symbol, is a mark reading Engine #19 - Ironforge Siege Brigade.",h="A metallic black box has turned up in a giant condor's stomach in the Badlands, its surface heavily pitted as...",sec={{t="Pulled from a Condor",b="The pitting suggests the box sat inside the condor for ages while acid ate at the metal. Turn it over and a symbol is stamped on the bottom, with Engine #19 - Ironforge Siege Brigade written below. You are to carry it to the Hall of Arms in Ironforge, to Pilot Longbeard.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where did the corroded black box come from?",a="It was in the stomach of a giant condor in the Badlands, and seems to have lain there a very long while.",al={"where did the box come from","how did the box get here","black box origin"}},{q="What markings are stamped on the box?",a="A symbol is stamped on the bottom, and beneath it is written Engine #19 - Ironforge Siege Brigade.",al={"what does the box say","markings on the black box","box inscription"}},{q="Who is supposed to receive the box?",a="Pilot Longbeard, at the Hall of Arms in Ironforge.",al={"who gets the box","where does the black box go","who do i bring the box to"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The box bears Ironforge's markings, and its trail ends in Ironforge."},kw={"badlands","black box","corroded black box","giant condor","hall of arms","ironforge siege brigade","pilot longbeard"},rel={"npc:pilot-longbeard","zone:ironforge","zone:badlands"},m={start="Corroded Black Box",["end"]="Pilot Longbeard",level="40",faction="Alliance",id=708},src={"The Black Box"}}
E["quest:710"] = {t="quest",n="Study of the Elements: Rock",z="badlands",s="Lotwil Veriatus has stopped in the Badlands to work on shackles of elemental binding. To test some offensive spells and a few pieced-together gizmos, Lotwil needs small stone shards from the lesser rock elementals nearby.",h="Lotwil Veriatus has stopped in the Badlands to work on shackles of elemental binding.",sec={{t="Elemental Shackles",b="Here in the Badlands, Lotwil Veriatus is working on a project: shackles of elemental binding. Once finished, they would let mages summon still stronger elementals for even greater uses. To get started, Lotwil wants ten small stone shards, easily taken from the lesser rock elementals in the hills immediately west.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is asking for the stone shards?",a="Lotwil Veriatus, who has stopped in the Badlands to work on a project.",al={"who gives this quest","quest giver","lotwil veriatus"}},{q="What is Lotwil Veriatus working on?",a="Shackles of elemental binding, meant to let mages summon even more powerful elementals.",al={"lotwil project","shackles of elemental binding","what is lotwil building"}},{q="Why does Lotwil need small stone shards?",a="They are for testing some of Lotwil's newest offensive spells and a few gizmos pieced together.",al={"why stone shards","shards purpose","what are shards for"}},{q="Where are the stone shards found?",a="From the lesser rock elementals in the hills immediately west of Lotwil.",al={"where to find shards","lesser rock elementals location","stone shard source"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Mages are the ones Lotwil's shackles are meant to serve."},kw={"badlands","lesser rock elementals","lotwil veriatus","shackles of elemental binding","small stone shards","study of the elements: rock"},rel={"npc:lotwil-veriatus","zone:badlands","topic:mage"},m={start="Lotwil Veriatus",["end"]="Lotwil Veriatus",level="37",faction="Neutral",id=710},src={"Study of the Elements: Rock"}}
E["quest:711"] = {t="quest",n="Study of the Elements: Rock",z="badlands",s="Lotwil Veriatus praises you as abler than all of Lotwil's apprentices combined, and wants the next step of the tests. This time the need is three large stone slabs, pieces best found on rock elementals.",h="Lotwil Veriatus praises you as abler than all of Lotwil's apprentices combined, and wants the next step of...",sec={{t="Bigger Pieces",b="The next parts of Lotwil Veriatus's work need more strength. Rock elementals have larger, sturdier bodies, so they are likelier to carry pieces big enough for the tests. Lotwil points you further west, or southeast along the edges of the mountains, and has you gather three large stone slabs. Lotwil needs a while to test the smaller pieces you brought before.",sp=0},{t="Lotwil's Hopes",b="Lotwil's spells acted on the smaller pieces just as predicted. If the next experiment goes as well as foreseen, the elementals under Lotwil's control would put anything summoned before to shame.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you after the large slabs?",a="Lotwil Veriatus, who is working in the Badlands.",al={"who gives this quest","lotwil quest","study of the elements giver"}},{q="What came before this request?",a="The earlier Study of the Elements: Rock, in which you brought Lotwil small stone shards.",al={"previous quest","prior step","what did i do before"}},{q="Where does Lotwil say to find the rock elementals?",a="Further west of Lotwil, or southeast along the edges of the mountains.",al={"where are the elementals","elemental locations","where to find slabs"}},{q="Why does Lotwil need larger stone slabs?",a="Lotwil needs larger pieces for the next tests. Rock elementals have bigger, stronger bodies, so their pieces are large enough.",al={"why large slabs","purpose of slabs","lotwil research goal"}}},kw={"badlands","large stone slabs","lotwil veriatus","rock elementals","stone slabs","study of the elements: rock"},rel={"npc:lotwil-veriatus","quest:710","zone:badlands","subzone:mirage-flats"},m={start="Lotwil Veriatus",["end"]="Lotwil Veriatus",level="39",faction="Neutral",id=711},src={"Study of the Elements: Rock (2)"}}
E["quest:712"] = {t="quest",n="Study of the Elements: Rock",z="badlands",s="Lotwil Veriatus needs one more part from the elementals of the Badlands: bracers of rock binding, taken from greater rock elementals. By Lotwil's reckoning they are enough to gauge the strength of Lotwil's own shackles.",h="Lotwil Veriatus needs one more part from the elementals of the Badlands: bracers of rock binding, taken from...",sec={{t="Gauging the Shackles",b="After the stone slabs, Lotwil Veriatus asks for one last part from the Badlands' elementals. Bracers of rock binding, taken from greater rock elementals, should let Lotwil judge the strength of the shackles under construction. Lotwil's scrying showed a group of the elementals southwest, near some ogres, if memory serves. Five bracers are wanted, so there are spares, since Servo is notorious for misplacing reagents and research.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Lotwil need the bracers?",a="By Lotwil's calculations, the bracers of rock binding are enough to gauge the strength of Lotwil's own shackles.",al={"why bracers of rock binding","what are bracers for","lotwil binding bracers"}},{q="Why does Lotwil ask for five bracers?",a="To have extras, because Servo is notorious for misplacing Lotwil's reagents and research.",al={"why five bracers","how many bracers","why extras"}},{q="Where are the greater rock elementals located?",a="A group of them lies southwest of Lotwil, near some ogres, according to Lotwil's scrying. The hills around Camp Cagg are home to them.",al={"where are rock elementals","greater rock elemental location","where to find bracers"}},{q="What becomes of the stone slabs collected earlier?",a="Lucien will take the extra slabs back to Kharanos once the work here is done, since they could prove useful again.",al={"what happened to stone slabs","lucien stone slabs","kharanos slabs"}}},kw={"badlands","bracers of rock binding","greater rock elementals","kharanos","lotwil veriatus","lucien","ogres","servo"},rel={"npc:lotwil-veriatus","zone:badlands","subzone:kharanos"},m={start="Lotwil Veriatus",["end"]="Lotwil Veriatus",level="42",faction="Neutral",id=712},src={"Study of the Elements: Rock (3)"}}
E["quest:713"] = {t="quest",n="Coolant Heads Prevail",z="badlands",s="Lotwil Veriatus wants a vial of Frost Oil to strengthen the shackles meant to hold a summoned friend in check. Bro'kin, a goblin friend of Lotwil's in Alterac, can teach you to make it.",h="Lotwil Veriatus wants a vial of Frost Oil to strengthen the shackles meant to hold a summoned friend in check.",sec={{t="A Vital Coolant",b="Lotwil Veriatus swears nothing keeps an engine or gears from overheating like Frost Oil, and that its worth as a lubricant is without equal. It also helps magical items hold on to their enchantments. A vial would raise the magical capacity of Lotwil's shackles, making them strong enough to stop the summoned friend from killing everyone.",sp=0},{t="Bro'kin of Alterac",b="Bro'kin, a goblin friend of Lotwil's, can teach you to make the oil. Bro'kin is in the Ruins of Alterac, and sells from a spot up on the wall of the old city.",sp=0},{t="When the Oil Arrives",b="Once the oil arrives, Lotwil calls it the perfect coolant for the new bracers. Lotwil swears that if the enchantments do not last a century, all Lotwil's belongings will go to Servo. Lotwil also expects the mages of the Assembly to be in awe when the work is finished.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Lotwil Veriatus need Frost Oil?",a="A vial would increase the magical capacity of Lotwil's shackles, so they are strong enough to stop the summoned friend from killing everyone.",al={"why frost oil","what is frost oil for","lotwil oil"}},{q="Who knows how to brew Frost Oil?",a="Bro'kin, a goblin friend of Lotwil's, can teach you to make it. He is in the Ruins of Alterac, up on a wall of the old city.",al={"who teaches frost oil","where to learn frost oil","brokin recipe"}},{q="What is special about Frost Oil?",a="Lotwil says nothing keeps an engine or gears from overheating like it, that it lasts as a lubricant without equal, and that it helps magical items hold on to enchantments.",al={"frost oil properties","why is frost oil good"}}},kw={"badlands","bro'kin","coolant heads prevail","frost oil","lotwil veriatus","ruins of alterac","shackles"},rel={"npc:lotwil-veriatus","zone:badlands","subzone:ruins-of-alterac","topic:goblin"},m={start="Lotwil Veriatus",["end"]="Lotwil Veriatus",level="37",faction="Neutral",id=713},src={"Coolant Heads Prevail"}}
E["quest:714"] = {t="quest",n="Gyro... What?",z="badlands",s="Having brought Lotwil Veriatus the Frost Oil from Coolant Heads Prevail, you find Lotwil still absorbed in a contraption in the Badlands. One small but crucial part is missing: a gyrochronatom.",h="Having brought Lotwil Veriatus the Frost Oil from Coolant Heads Prevail, you find Lotwil still absorbed in a...",sec={{t="A Crucial Part",b="Lotwil Veriatus, distracted by the work, says you have done the job well beyond all standards and tells you to come and apply for work if you ever meet in Kharanos. Then comes a hurried scramble to catch hold of something, and the real request: a gyrochronatom. It is a small part, Lotwil admits, but a crucial one. Bring one and the project should be ready to complete.",sp=0},{t="Handing It Over",b="When you hand the gyrochronatom over, Lotwil seizes it with a shout and says the work is nearly done, truly, and that this project is the top priority at the moment. The promise to finish soon keeps wobbling, from a few minutes to maybe a lot longer.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is asking for the gyrochronatom?",a="Lotwil Veriatus, who is working on a contraption in the Badlands.",al={"who gives gyro what","gyro what quest giver","lotwil veriatus badlands"}},{q="What does Lotwil Veriatus need the gyrochronatom for?",a="It is a small but rather crucial part, and with it Lotwil should be ready to complete the project.",al={"why gyrochronatom","what is lotwil building"}},{q="What is the offer about Kharanos?",a="Distracted by the work, Lotwil says that if you ever meet in Kharanos, you are free to come and apply for work.",al={"lotwil kharanos","kharanos job offer"}},{q="Where can a gyrochronatom be found?",a="Engineers make them, and they can also be bought from engineering suppliers.",al={"how to get gyrochronatom","gyrochronatom source","where buy gyrochronatom"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Engineers can make a gyrochronatom themselves."},kw={"badlands","contraption","coolant heads prevail","gyrochronatom","kharanos","lotwil veriatus"},rel={"npc:lotwil-veriatus","quest:713","zone:badlands","subzone:kharanos"},m={start="Lotwil Veriatus",["end"]="Lotwil Veriatus",level="37",id=714},src={"Gyro... What?"}}
E["quest:716"] = {t="quest",n="Stone Is Better than Cloth",z="badlands",s="Lucien Tosselwrench knows how cheap Lotwil can be, and offers to make something for your trouble: enchanted bracers built from the extra stones you collected. What Lucien lacks is a blacksmith's patterned bronze bracers.",h="Lucien Tosselwrench knows how cheap Lotwil can be, and offers to make something for your trouble: enchanted...",sec={{t="A Thank-You for Your Trouble",b="After the Study of the Elements: Rock trials, Lucien Tosselwrench admits how cheap Lotwil can be and wants to make it up to you. Lucien has been busy with the extra stones you gathered and can make fine enchanted bracers. They may even help guard you against what Lucien calls the coming atrocity of Lotwil's newest invention.",sp=0},{t="What Lucien Needs",b="To finish the bracers, Lucien needs patterned bronze bracers, the kind a blacksmith makes. Lucien warns that it is wise not to wait long, since no one knows what happens next.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who offers to craft the bracers?",a="Lucien Tosselwrench, in the Badlands, offers to make enchanted bracers from the extra stones you collected.",al={"who gives stone is better than cloth","quest giver","lucien tosselwrench"}},{q="Why is Lucien making this armor for you?",a="Lucien knows how cheap Lotwil can be and wants to make something for all your troubles. It may also help protect you from Lotwil's newest invention.",al={"why make bracers","lucien motive","lotwil cheap"}},{q="What does Lucien need to finish crafting the bracers?",a="Patterned bronze bracers, the kind a blacksmith makes.",al={"what item is needed","required items","patterned bronze bracers needed"}},{q="What comes before this quest?",a="It follows Lotwil's third Study of the Elements: Rock request.",al={"previous quest","prerequisite for stone is better than cloth"}}},ang={["profession:Blacksmithing"]="The bronze bracers Lucien wants come from a blacksmith."},kw={"badlands","elemental rock","enchanted bracers","lotwil veriatus","lucien tosselwrench","patterned bronze bracers"},rel={"quest:712","zone:badlands"},m={start="Lucien Tosselwrench",["end"]="Lucien Tosselwrench",level="42",faction="Neutral",id=716},src={"Stone Is Better than Cloth"}}
E["quest:717"] = {t="quest",n="Tremors of the Earth",z="badlands",s="Garek has concluded that Blacklash and Hematus cannot be trusted to stay in their prison at Lethlor. Black dragons have moved in there and ogres took the Sign of the Earth, so Garek sends you to free the drakes and kill them.",h="Garek has concluded that Blacklash and Hematus cannot be trusted to stay in their prison at Lethlor.",sec={{t="A Prison Failing",b="Garek can no longer be sure Blacklash and Hematus will stay imprisoned. Black dragons now dwell at Lethlor, and ogres have made off with the Sign of the Earth. Garek judges that something harsher is needed, and the drakes must die.",sp=0},{t="Breaking the Seal",b="Three runestones keep the drakes locked away, and only the Sign of the Earth can fetch them. You use the Sign on the Pillars of Amethyst, Opal and Diamond, then set the runestones into the Seal of the Earth. That frees the pair, and you slay them. Garek wants back Blacklash's Bindings, the Chains of Hematus and the Sign of the Earth.",sp=0},{t="After the Deed",b="Once the drakes are dead, Garek declares that the Kirin Tor can stop fretting over Lethlor's prisoners. Garek means to report success to a master, Krasus, who will surely be pleased.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who are Blacklash and Hematus?",a="Drakes held prisoner in Lethlor, behind a seal.",al={"blacklash and hematus","who are the drakes","what is imprisoned in lethlor"}},{q="Why must the drakes be killed instead of kept locked away?",a="Garek can no longer be sure they will stay imprisoned. Black dragons now live at Lethlor, and ogres took the Sign of the Earth.",al={"why kill blacklash","why break the prison","why slay hematus"}},{q="How is the prison unsealed?",a="Three runestones are taken from the pillars with the Sign of the Earth, then placed in the Seal of the Earth.",al={"how to open seal of the earth","how to summon blacklash","how to break the drakes out"}},{q="What must be brought back to Garek?",a="Three things go back to Garek: Blacklash's Bindings, the Chains of Hematus and the Sign of the Earth, each from a different pillar.",al={"what to return to garek","blacklash's bindings","chains of hematus"}},{q="What comes before this quest?",a="It follows the earlier Tremors of the Earth.",al={"previous quest","prerequisite for tremors of the earth"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Garek's request is one for the Alliance."},kw={"blacklash","garek","hematus","kirin tor","krasus","lethlor ravine","runestones","seal of the earth","sign of the earth","tremors of the earth"},rel={"zone:badlands","subzone:lethlor-ravine"},m={start="Garek",["end"]="Garek",level="50",faction="Alliance",id=717},src={"Tremors of the Earth (2)"}}
E["quest:718"] = {t="quest",n="Mirages",z="badlands",s="Hurrying away from the Uldaman excavation site, Sigrun Ironhew's party left wagons and crates behind. Ogres from Camp Kosh took the cart holding all their weapons, and since then the party has had no food.",h="Hurrying away from the Uldaman excavation site, Sigrun Ironhew's party left wagons and crates behind.",sec={{t="Hungry in the Badlands",b="In their rush to leave the Uldaman excavation site, Sigrun Ironhew and company left many wagons and supply crates behind. Ogres from Camp Kosh have been picking over the leftovers like vultures. They took the cart holding all the party's weapons, and since then the party has had no food. Sigrun admits it is embarrassing and asks you to retrieve the supply crate.",sp=0},{t="On Your Return",b="When you come back, Sigrun confesses to having swallowed a mouthful of sand while you were away. Sigrun quickly moves on, saying the party will go out and find food tonight and eat like kings.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Sigrun Ironhew?",a="Sigrun Ironhew belongs to a party that left the Uldaman excavation site in a hurry and is now without food in the Badlands.",al={"sigrun ironhew","who gives mirages","who is sigrun"}},{q="Why is Sigrun's party starving?",a="Ogres took the cart that carried all their weapons and such, and since then they have been unable to get any food.",al={"why are they hungry","why no food","sigrun food problem"}},{q="Who took the abandoned supplies?",a="The local ogres from Camp Kosh, who have been all over the equipment left behind.",al={"who stole the crate","camp kosh ogres","who took weapons"}},{q="What is Sigrun hoping to get back?",a="The supply crate, left behind in the rush to leave the excavation site.",al={"supply crate","what to retrieve for sigrun"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Sigrun Ironhew is looking for Alliance help."},kw={"badlands","camp kosh","excavation","mirages","ogres","sigrun ironhew","supply crate","uldaman"},rel={"zone:badlands","subzone:camp-kosh","subzone:uldaman"},m={start="Sigrun Ironhew",["end"]="Sigrun Ironhew",level="38",faction="Alliance",id=718},src={"Mirages"}}
E["quest:719"] = {t="quest",n="A Dwarf and His Tools",z="badlands",s="Prospector Ryedol warns that Dark Iron dwarves, looking like the Shadowforge clan, are all around. They just attacked the dig site where Ryedol worked, and Ryedol wants the lucky pick back.",h="Prospector Ryedol warns that Dark Iron dwarves, looking like the Shadowforge clan, are all around.",sec={{t="Raiders at the Dig",b="Dark Iron dwarves of the Shadowforge clan, by Prospector Ryedol's account, have attacked the excavation site where Ryedol worked. They killed nearly everyone, Ryedol's boss Hammertoe among them, and Ryedol barely escaped with life intact. The site lies to the north of Ryedol's position.",sp=0},{t="A Lucky Pick",b="Ryedol is working out how to win back some of the lost supplies, above all his lucky pick. One of the Dark Iron must be carrying it, though it could be any of them. Ryedol hopes you will help, and waits south of Hammertoe's Dig Site.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Prospector Ryedol?",a="Ryedol worked at an excavation site that Dark Iron dwarves attacked. He barely escaped and now waits south of Hammertoe's Dig Site.",al={"who is ryedol","prospector ryedol","who gives a dwarf and his tools"}},{q="Who attacked the excavation camp?",a="Dark Iron dwarves who looked to be of the Shadowforge clan.",al={"who attacked the dig","who attacked hammertoe","what attacked the camp"}},{q="What happened to Hammertoe?",a="Hammertoe was Ryedol's boss, and was among those killed in the attack.",al={"who is hammertoe","is hammertoe alive","what happened to boss hammertoe"}},{q="Where is the lucky pick located?",a="Ryedol believes one of the Dark Iron has it, though it could be any of them.",al={"where is ryedols lucky pick","how to find the pick","who has ryedols pick"}}},kw={"badlands","dark iron","excavation","hammertoe","lucky pick","ryedol","shadowforge"},rel={"npc:prospector-ryedol","zone:badlands"},m={start="Prospector Ryedol",["end"]="Prospector Ryedol",level="35",faction="Alliance",id=719},src={"A Dwarf and His Tools"}}
E["quest:720"] = {t="quest",n="A Sign of Hope",z="badlands",s="A crumpled map bears a few words scrawled in chalk: a plea to Ryedol from Hammertoe, who says they are taking Hammertoe to Uldaman and asks for help. Prospector Ryedol should hear that Hammertoe Grez lives.",h="A crumpled map bears a few words scrawled in chalk: a plea to Ryedol from Hammertoe, who says they are taking...",sec={{t="Words in Chalk",b="Roughly scribbled in chalk on the crumpled map is a short note signed by Hammertoe. It is addressed to Ryedol and says only that they are taking Hammertoe to Uldaman and that help is needed. The word to carry to Prospector Ryedol is that Hammertoe Grez lives.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is written on the crumpled map?",a="A note in chalk, addressed to Ryedol and signed Hammertoe. It says they are taking Hammertoe to Uldaman and asks for help.",al={"what does the note say","chalk message on map","crumpled map text"}},{q="Who is Prospector Ryedol?",a="The one the note is meant for. You are to seek out Prospector Ryedol and tell him that Hammertoe Grez lives.",al={"who is ryedol","where to bring crumpled map"}},{q="Where does the message say Hammertoe Grez is being taken?",a="To Uldaman.",al={"where is hammertoe taken","where is grez taken"}}},kw={"a sign of hope","badlands","chalk note","crumpled map","hammertoe grez","prospector ryedol","uldaman"},rel={"npc:prospector-ryedol","subzone:uldaman","zone:badlands"},m={start="Crumpled Map",["end"]="Prospector Ryedol",level="35",faction="Alliance",id=720},src={"A Sign of Hope"}}
E["quest:723"] = {t="quest",n="Prospect of Faith",z="badlands",s="Hammertoe Grez, nursing wounds, sends you with the amulet to Prospector Ryedol in the Badlands. Ryedol knows what Hammertoe was seeking, and what the Shadowforge clan must not be allowed to find.",h="Hammertoe Grez, nursing wounds, sends you with the amulet to Prospector Ryedol in the Badlands.",sec={{t="An Amulet for Ryedol",b="Hammertoe Grez, clutching at wounds, pauses to steady himself, then asks you to find Ryedol and hand over the amulet. Hammertoe is sure Ryedol will figure out what to do. Ryedol knows Hammertoe was seeking the origins of their people, and that Hammertoe also meant to thwart the Shadowforge clan, who cannot be permitted to get hold of the scrolls.",sp=0},{t="At Ryedol's Hands",b="Ryedol, on receiving Hammertoe's amulet, says that spirits were higher when Hammertoe was thought dead, since knowing for sure only makes the pain worse. Ryedol calls the amulet Hammertoe's life's work and vows that the death will not be in vain.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Prospector Ryedol?",a="Prospector Ryedol is the one you are to bring Hammertoe's amulet to, in the Badlands. Ryedol knows what Hammertoe was seeking.",al={"prospector ryedol","who is ryedol","where is ryedol"}},{q="What is Hammertoe Grez trying to stop?",a="Hammertoe wanted to thwart the Shadowforge clan, who cannot be permitted to get hold of the scrolls.",al={"hammertoe purpose","shadowforge scrolls","why stop shadowforge"}},{q="What was Hammertoe Grez seeking?",a="The origins of their people, according to Hammertoe.",al={"hammertoe origins","what was hammertoe looking for"}},{q="Which chain is this step part of?",a="This is part of the chain that began with A Sign of Hope.",al={"prospect of faith chain","a sign of hope chain"}}},kw={"a sign of hope","badlands","hammertoe grez","hammertoes amulet","origins","prospector ryedol","shadowforge"},rel={"npc:prospector-ryedol","zone:badlands"},m={start="Hammertoe Grez",["end"]="Prospector Ryedol",level="40",faction="Alliance",id=723},src={"Prospect of Faith"}}
E["quest:724"] = {t="quest",n="Prospect of Faith",z="badlands",s="Prospector Ryedol sends you to Ironforge with Hammertoe's Amulet. Historian Karnik and Hammertoe were working together to find the lost artifacts of Uldaman, and Ryedol guesses the Shadowforge found out the pair knew more than they let on.",h="Prospector Ryedol sends you to Ironforge with Hammertoe's Amulet.",sec={{t="A Message for Ironforge",b="Ryedol sorts through who might know what to do next and settles on Historian Karnik, who is in Ironforge. You are to tell Karnik what has happened to Hammertoe and place the amulet in the historian's hands. Karnik will say what needs doing from there.",sp=0},{t="Karnik's Welcome",b="Karnik greets you as just another traveler asking for time and has none to spare, until the amulet is shown. Then Karnik takes the matter seriously, puts mourning for Hammertoe aside for later, and shows you why the amulet is worth so much by calling up Hammertoe's spirit.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who starts this quest?",a="Prospector Ryedol in the Badlands sends you on to Ironforge with Hammertoe's Amulet.",al={"who gives prospect of faith","prospect of faith questgiver","where to start prospect of faith"}},{q="Where is Historian Karnik located?",a="Historian Karnik is in Ironforge.",al={"where is karnik","historian karnik location","karnik ironforge"}},{q="Why was Historian Karnik chosen?",a="Karnik and Hammertoe were working together to find the lost artifacts of Uldaman, so Ryedol trusts Karnik to know what to do.",al={"why send the amulet to karnik","karnik connection"}},{q="What comes after this quest?",a="Karnik's part of the story carries on with Passing Word of a Threat.",al={"next quest after prospect of faith","what follows prospect of faith"}}},kw={"badlands","hammertoe","hammertoes amulet","historian karnik","ironforge","prospect of faith","prospector ryedol","shadowforge","uldaman"},rel={"npc:prospector-ryedol","zone:ironforge","quest:725","quest:723","quest:720","subzone:uldaman","zone:badlands"},m={start="Prospector Ryedol",["end"]="Historian Karnik",level="40",faction="Alliance",id=724},src={"Prospect of Faith (2)"}}
E["quest:725"] = {t="quest",n="Passing Word of a Threat",z="badlands",s="Historian Karnik gives you a sealed note for Advisor Belgrum. You are to tell Belgrum what you have witnessed and ask how Belgrum wants to proceed, while Karnik turns to Hammertoe's spirit about the Shadowforge in the Badlands.",h="Historian Karnik gives you a sealed note for Advisor Belgrum.",sec={{t="Word for Advisor Belgrum",b="Karnik wants you to find Advisor Belgrum quickly, tell what you have seen, and ask how Belgrum wants to proceed. The note explains more. Meanwhile Karnik will speak with Hammertoe's spirit, hoping Hammertoe knows something that could put an end to the Shadowforge's doings in the Badlands, and can only pray that it does.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you to Advisor Belgrum?",a="Historian Karnik hands you a sealed note and asks you to find Advisor Belgrum as fast as you can.",al={"who starts passing word of a threat","who gives passing word of a threat","karnik quest"}},{q="What does Karnik want from Advisor Belgrum?",a="Karnik wants Belgrum told what you have witnessed and asked how Belgrum wants to proceed. The note explains more.",al={"why visit belgrum","belgrum note purpose","why send the note"}},{q="What is Historian Karnik doing while you deliver the note?",a="Karnik takes the time to speak with Hammertoe's spirit, hoping to learn something that helps stop the Shadowforge in the Badlands.",al={"what does karnik do","karnik plan","historian karnik badlands"}},{q="What quest comes before Passing Word of a Threat?",a="It follows Prospect of Faith, the step in which you bring Hammertoe's amulet to Karnik in Ironforge.",al={"passing word prerequisite","passing word of a threat previous quest","prior quest"}}},kw={"advisor belgrum","badlands","hammertoe","historian karnik","ironforge","passing word of a threat","shadowforge"},rel={"quest:723","quest:720","zone:badlands"},m={start="Historian Karnik",["end"]="Advisor Belgrum",level="40",faction="Alliance",id=725},src={"Passing Word of a Threat"}}
E["quest:726"] = {t="quest",n="Passing Word of a Threat",z="badlands",s="Advisor Belgrum has read Historian Karnik's note and sends you back to Karnik with a message spoken on the king's authority: act on what is known, swiftly and decisively, and halt the Shadowforge's doings in the Badlands.",h="Advisor Belgrum has read Historian Karnik's note and sends you back to Karnik with a message spoken on the...",sec={{t="Belgrum's Answer",b="Belgrum reads to the end of the note with widening eyes and calls the tidings evil. You are to return to Karnik and relay, on the king's authority, that the information must be acted on quickly and decisively. The Shadowforge's activities in the Badlands have to stop.",sp=0},{t="Karnik's Reply",b="Karnik takes the urgency as the king's own and has a plan ready: the Shadowforge in Uldaman can be slowed by a blow against Angor Fortress, from which they run their operations.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you back to Karnik?",a="Advisor Belgrum, after reading Karnik's note. You carry a message on the king's authority to act swiftly and decisively.",al={"who gives the order","belgrum orders","royal authority badlands"}},{q="What does Belgrum want done about the Shadowforge?",a="Belgrum wants Karnik to act quickly and firmly, and to put an end to what the Shadowforge are doing in the Badlands.",al={"what does belgrum want","shadowforge badlands order"}},{q="What came before this?",a="You brought Karnik's sealed note to Advisor Belgrum in the earlier Passing Word of a Threat, which followed the Prospect of Faith steps.",al={"previous step","quest before passing word of a threat","badlands lead up"}}},kw={"angor fortress","badlands","belgrum","karnik","shadowforge","uldaman"},rel={"quest:725","quest:762","zone:badlands","subzone:uldaman","quest:723","quest:720"},m={start="Advisor Belgrum",["end"]="Historian Karnik",level="40",faction="Alliance",id=726},src={"Passing Word of a Threat (2)"}}
E["quest:727"] = {t="quest",n="To Ironforge for Yagyin's Digest",z="badlands",s="Theldurin the Lost sends you to Ironforge with a sigil. In a shop in the Forlorn Cavern, Gerrig Bonegrip is to take you for one of the people Theldurin fled, and you are to ask Gerrig for Yagyin's Digest.",h="Theldurin the Lost sends you to Ironforge with a sigil.",sec={{t="A Book Written Long Ago",b="The Tablet tells Theldurin much, but not nearly enough. Yagyin wrote a digest in ages past, and the people Theldurin fled keep copies in many places, with their most learned studying it. Theldurin believes it holds vast knowledge that can offer protection, and wants it brought back.",sp=0},{t="The Shop in the Forlorn Cavern",b="Gerrig Bonegrip keeps a shop in the Forlorn Cavern of Ironforge. Theldurin gives you the Sigil of the Hammer to show Gerrig, so that you will be taken for one of them, and you are to ask for Yagyin's Digest.",sp=0},{t="Gerrig's Greeting",b="Gerrig warns you to watch what you touch in the shop, for knowledge can be deadly. When the sigil is shown, Gerrig greets you as brother or sister and offers praise to the dwellers beneath.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Theldurin want Yagyin's Digest?",a="The Tablet tells Theldurin much but not enough. The digest, written by Yagyin in ages past, holds vast knowledge that can offer protection, and Theldurin wants it brought back.",al={"why need yagyins digest","what is yagyins digest","yagyin digest purpose"}},{q="Where is Gerrig Bonegrip?",a="Gerrig Bonegrip is found at a shop in Ironforge's Forlorn Cavern.",al={"where is gerrig bonegrip","gerrig bonegrip location","who is gerrig"}},{q="What is the Sigil of the Hammer used for?",a="Theldurin gives it to you to show Gerrig Bonegrip, so that Gerrig will think you one of the people Theldurin fled.",al={"what does the sigil do","sigil of the hammer use","why use the sigil"}},{q="Where does this fit in the chain?",a="It comes after Solution to Doom, with Theldurin the Lost, and carries on in the next step of the chain.",al={"what comes before to ironforge for yagyins digest","chain order yagyin"}}},kw={"badlands","forlorn cavern","gerrig bonegrip","ironforge","sigil of the hammer","theldurin the lost","yagyin's digest"},rel={"npc:theldurin-the-lost","npc:gerrig-bonegrip","subzone:forlorn-cavern","zone:ironforge","zone:badlands"},m={start="Theldurin the Lost",["end"]="Gerrig Bonegrip",level="40",faction="Alliance",id=727},src={"To Ironforge for Yagyin's Digest"}}
E["quest:728"] = {t="quest",n="To the Undercity for Yagyin's Digest",z="badlands",s="Theldurin the Lost sends you to the Undercity of Lordaeron with a sigil. Keeper Bel'dugur is to take you for one of the people Theldurin fled, and you are to ask the keeper for Yagyin's Digest.",h="Theldurin the Lost sends you to the Undercity of Lordaeron with a sigil.",sec={{t="A Book Written Long Ago",b="The tablet tells Theldurin much, but not nearly enough. Yagyin wrote a digest in ages past, and the people Theldurin fled keep copies in many places, with their most learned studying it. Theldurin believes it holds vast knowledge that can protect them, and wants it brought back.",sp=0},{t="The Keeper in the Undercity",b="Keeper Bel'dugur is in the Undercity of Lordaeron. Theldurin gives you the Sigil of the Hammer to show the keeper, so that you will be taken for one of them, and you are to ask for the digest.",sp=0},{t="A Word of Caution",b="Bel'dugur greets you as an eager seeker of the collection and warns that knowledge gives power to the strong but drives the weak mad. Once the sigil is shown, Bel'dugur urges you to be discreet with such signs. Some do not believe in the righteousness of their pledge, and others would see them fail if they knew of them. Those who share the pledge must always be careful, watchful and patient.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to the Undercity?",a="Theldurin the Lost sends you, with the Sigil of the Hammer, to find Keeper Bel'dugur.",al={"who starts this quest","who gives to the undercity for yagyin's digest","quest giver"}},{q="What is the Sigil of the Hammer for?",a="Theldurin gives it to you to show Keeper Bel'dugur, so that the keeper will think you one of the people Theldurin fled.",al={"sigil of the hammer use","why do i need the sigil","what does the sigil do"}},{q="What is Yagyin's Digest?",a="It is a book Yagyin wrote in ages past. Theldurin says it holds vast knowledge and is studied by the most learned of the people Theldurin fled.",al={"what is yagyins digest","who is yagyin","yagyin book"}},{q="Where is Keeper Bel'dugur?",a="Keeper Bel'dugur stays in the Undercity of Lordaeron, where you find the Keeper.",al={"keeper bel'dugur location","where to find keeper beldugur","beldugur undercity"}},{q="What came before this?",a="It follows Solution to Doom.",al={"previous quest","what comes before this","solution to doom connection"}}},kw={"badlands","bel'dugur","digest","hammer","sigil","theldurin","undercity","yagyin"},rel={"npc:theldurin-the-lost","npc:keeper-bel-dugur","zone:undercity","quest:736","zone:badlands","topic:lordaeron"},m={start="Theldurin the Lost",["end"]="Keeper Bel'dugur",level="40",faction="Horde",id=728},src={"To the Undercity for Yagyin's Digest"}}
E["quest:732"] = {t="quest",n="Tremors of the Earth",z="badlands",s="Garek has heard from Sigrun how much you have helped, and asks for your help in turn. Garek's master, Krasus of the Kirin Tor, sent Garek to stop whatever is brewing in Lethlor Ravine, and first a stolen Sign of the Earth must be found.",h="Garek has heard from Sigrun how much you have helped, and asks for your help in turn.",sec={{t="A Matter Kept Close",b="Garek was sent to the Badlands by Krasus of the Kirin Tor, Garek's master, to stop the trouble that is brewing in Lethlor Ravine. The exact assignment cannot be shared, only that it matters greatly. A band of roving ogres, now and then spotted around Camp Boff, took the Sign of the Earth, and Garek needs it. Bring it back and there will be more to learn.",sp=0},{t="The Wandering Ogres",b="The ogres move from camp to camp across the Badlands, and rising heat and swirling winds make their trail hard to follow. Garek has heard they sometimes pass through Camp Boff, a fair place to look if you lose track of them.",sp=0},{t="Garek Explains",b="When you return with the Sign, Garek tells you that Dark Iron dwarves of Angor Fortress made it in order to bind Deathwing's twin lieutenants, the ruthless Blacklash and Hematus.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Garek working for?",a="Garek's master is Krasus of the Kirin Tor, who sent Garek to the Badlands to stop the trouble brewing in Lethlor Ravine.",al={"who sent garek","garek master","krasus badlands"}},{q="What is the Sign of the Earth?",a="Wandering ogres stole it and Garek needs it back. Garek will say more once you bring it.",al={"sign of the earth","what is the sign of the earth","sign of earth lore"}},{q="Where can the wandering ogres be found?",a="They roam between their camps across the Badlands, and Garek has heard they sometimes pass through Camp Boff.",al={"where are the ogres","ogre camp boff","where is sign of the earth"}},{q="Why does Garek keep the assignment secret?",a="Garek will not say what the assignment is or what work it calls for, only that it is vitally important.",al={"why secret","garek secret assignment"}}},kw={"angor fortress","camp boff","dark iron","deathwing","garek","kirin tor","krasus","lethlor ravine","sign of the earth"},rel={"zone:badlands","subzone:lethlor-ravine","quest:718","npc:deathwing"},m={start="Garek",["end"]="Garek",level="43",faction="Alliance",id=732},src={"Tremors of the Earth"}}
E["quest:733"] = {t="quest",n="Scrounging",z="badlands",s="Sigrun Ironhew needs materials to build defenses and other necessities for the camp, and has noticed the ogres nearby carry plenty of scrap metal. Sigrun wants seven pieces of it.",h="Sigrun Ironhew needs materials to build defenses and other necessities for the camp, and has noticed the...",sec={{t="A Camp Short of Materials",b="Sigrun finds it hard going without materials for defenses and other necessities, and the Prospector has been worrying about the state of the little camp. Sigrun wants to get to work soon, and needs scrap metal to do it.",sp=0},{t="The Ogres' Scrap",b="The ogres in the area seem well supplied with scrap metal, which makes Sigrun think the talk of siege engines in the Badlands may have had something to it. Their main camp is Dustbelch Grotto, a long trek west of Sigrun's camp.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is asking for the scrap metal?",a="Sigrun Ironhew, who wants it to build defenses and other necessities for the camp.",al={"quest giver","who gives scrounging","sigrun"}},{q="Why does the camp need scrap metal?",a="Sigrun lacks the materials to build defenses and other necessities, and the Prospector has been worrying about the state of the camp.",al={"why need scrap metal","purpose of scrap metal","defenses"}},{q="Where can the scrap metal be found?",a="The ogres in the area carry it. Their main camp is Dustbelch Grotto, a long trek west of Sigrun's camp.",al={"scrap metal location","where to get scrap metal","ogre camp"}},{q="What comes before this?",a="It follows Mirages.",al={"previous quest","scrounging prerequisite"}}},kw={"badlands","dustbelch grotto","explorers' league","ironforge","ogres","scrap metal","scrounging","sigrun ironhew"},rel={"quest:718","zone:badlands"},m={start="Sigrun Ironhew",["end"]="Sigrun Ironhew",level="40",faction="Alliance",id=733},src={"Scrounging"}}
E["quest:734"] = {t="quest",n="This Is Going to Be Hard",z="badlands",s="Lotwil Veriatus, busy with a set of shackles, sends you to speak with Lucien Tosselwrench in the Badlands. Lotwil needs a cog #5 and wants it brought back.",h="Lotwil Veriatus, busy with a set of shackles, sends you to speak with Lucien Tosselwrench in the Badlands.",sec={{t="Cog Number Five",b="Lotwil glances up at you briefly, then bends over the shackles again. You are to go and speak to Lucien Tosselwrench, because Lotwil needs a cog #5 and asks you to bring it.",sp=0},{t="Lucien's Verdict",b="At the mention of cog #5, Lucien Tosselwrench is not hopeful about how things will go.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives this quest?",a="Lotwil Veriatus, who is working on a set of shackles in the Badlands.",al={"who starts this quest","lotwil veriatus quest","quest giver"}},{q="What does Lotwil need?",a="A cog #5, which Lotwil asks you to bring back after speaking with Lucien Tosselwrench.",al={"what does lotwil want","which cog","cog 5"}},{q="Who do I speak to about the cog?",a="Lotwil sends you to Lucien Tosselwrench in the Badlands.",al={"where to find cog 5","who is lucien","lucien tosselwrench"}}},kw={"badlands","cog #5","lotwil veriatus","lucien tosselwrench","shackles"},rel={"npc:lotwil-veriatus","zone:badlands"},m={start="Lotwil Veriatus",["end"]="Lucien Tosselwrench",level="42",faction="Neutral",id=734},src={"This Is Going to Be Hard"}}
E["quest:735"] = {t="quest",n="The Star, the Hand and the Heart",z="badlands",s="Gerrig Bonegrip in Ironforge has a spare copy of Yagyin's Digest and will part with it for three items of power. Gerrig will not speak their names aloud, and writes them down in a note instead.",h="Gerrig Bonegrip in Ironforge has a spare copy of Yagyin's Digest and will part with it for three items of...",sec={{t="An Exchange Behind Closed Lips",b="Gerrig hears you ask for Yagyin's Digest and wonders whether you are starting a new chapter of their order somewhere, then decides it is not Gerrig's place to ask. Gerrig has an extra copy and believes those of the order must aid each other. In return, three items of power must be brought. Their names stay unspoken, since someone may be listening, and Gerrig writes them down.",sp=0},{t="The Three Items",b="The note names the Star of Xil'yeh, the Hand of Dagun and the Legacy Heart. They are what Gerrig wants before handing over the digest.",sp=0},{t="Gerrig's Verdict",b="Once the relics are in hand, Gerrig calls you resourceful and believes that, should founding a new chapter of the order truly be your charge, you will run it well.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who asks for the three items?",a="Gerrig Bonegrip in Ironforge, who has an extra copy of Yagyin's Digest to give in return.",al={"quest giver","who starts the star the hand and the heart","gerrig bonegrip quest"}},{q="What three items does Gerrig Bonegrip want?",a="Gerrig Bonegrip's note asks for three things: the Star of Xil'yeh, the Hand of Dagun and the Legacy Heart.",al={"required items","what relics does he need","bonegrips note items"}},{q="Why does Gerrig write the items down instead of saying them?",a="Gerrig will not speak their names because someone may be listening.",al={"why write them down","why the secret note","bonegrip whispers"}},{q="What came before this in the chain?",a="It follows To Ironforge for Yagyin's Digest, where Theldurin the Lost sent you to Gerrig.",al={"prerequisite quest","previous quest"}}},kw={"bonegrip's note","gerrig bonegrip","hand of dagun","ironforge","legacy heart","star of xil'yeh","yagyin's digest"},rel={"npc:gerrig-bonegrip","quest:727","zone:ironforge","zone:badlands"},m={start="Gerrig Bonegrip",["end"]="Gerrig Bonegrip",level="44",faction="Alliance",id=735},src={"The Star, the Hand and the Heart (Alliance)"}}
E["quest:737"] = {t="quest",n="Forbidden Knowledge",z="badlands",s="Yagyin's Digest is handed over with a warning to guard it well from unfriendly hands. Theldurin the Lost is the one to carry it to.",h="Yagyin's Digest is handed over with a warning to guard it well from unfriendly hands.",sec={{t="A Book That Burns",b="Gerrig Bonegrip in Ironforge, or Keeper Bel'dugur in the Undercity, gives you the digest. You are cautioned to guard it well and keep it away from unfriendly hands, for it carries many truths and truth has a way of burning. Carry it to Theldurin the Lost.",sp=0},{t="Theldurin's Hope",b="Theldurin cries out that hope glimmers and says your efforts may yet save them all, with a monument, a shrine and your name praised for generations to come. All of it holds only as long as THEY are not freed to rise to the surface, in which case, Theldurin says, everyone is worm food.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What item needs to be delivered?",a="Yagyin's Digest, a book that holds many truths. It must be guarded closely and kept from unfriendly hands.",al={"what book is this","what is yagyin's digest","what do i bring"}},{q="Who receives the digest?",a="The digest is meant for Theldurin the Lost.",al={"who gets the book","who do i turn this into","where does the digest go"}},{q="What came before this?",a="It follows the step in which three items were fetched in exchange for the digest.",al={"previous quest","what leads to this","what quest comes before forbidden knowledge"}}},kw={"badlands","forbidden knowledge","the star the hand and the heart","theldurin the lost","yagyin's digest"},rel={"npc:theldurin-the-lost","zone:badlands"},m={["end"]="Theldurin the Lost",level="40",faction="Both",id=737},src={"Forbidden Knowledge (Classic)"}}
E["quest:738"] = {t="quest",n="Find Agmond",z="badlands",s="Prospector Ironband has not heard from Prospector Agmond in weeks. Agmond was in charge of the excavation sites in the Badlands, and Ironband wants Agmond found so the report can be collected.",h="Prospector Ironband has not heard from Prospector Agmond in weeks.",sec={{t="A Silent Prospector",b="Agmond ran the excavations in the Badlands, to the southwest. Ironband says \"ran\" on purpose, for there has been no word from Agmond in weeks. Ironband wants Agmond found, and the report with him. Agmond was last heard of at the farthest-south dig of the Badlands, a small outfit beyond Angor Fortress, and that is where the search should begin.",sp=0},{t="Where the Trail Ends",b="At the end of the search you find a skeleton, which must be what is left of Agmond. The body is broken and battered, and the bones have been picked clean.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Prospector Agmond?",a="Agmond ran the excavations in the Badlands, southwest of Prospector Ironband.",al={"who is agmond","who agmond","agmond lore"}},{q="Why is Prospector Ironband looking for Agmond?",a="Ironband has not heard from Agmond in weeks and wants to get Agmond's report.",al={"why find agmond","ironband looking for agmond"}},{q="Where was Prospector Agmond last known to be?",a="At the farthest-south dig of the Badlands, a small outfit beyond Angor Fortress.",al={"agmond location","where is agmond dig site","where was agmond"}},{q="What comes before this in the chain?",a="It follows Ironband Wants You!",al={"previous quest","prereq for find agmond"}}},kw={"agmond","angor fortress","badlands","ironforge","prospector ironband"},rel={"npc:prospector-ironband","quest:739","zone:badlands","zone:ironforge"},m={start="Prospector Ironband",["end"]="Battered Dwarven Skeleton",level="38",faction="Alliance",id=738},src={"Find Agmond"}}
E["quest:739"] = {t="quest",n="Murdaloc",z="badlands",s="Agmond's battered remains lie in the Badlands, and a name is scrawled in the sandstone beside the dead hand: Murdaloc. Agmond's killer is to be put down, with word carried back to Prospector Ironband in Loch Modan.",h="Agmond's battered remains lie in the Badlands, and a name is scrawled in the sandstone beside the dead hand...",sec={{t="A Name in the Sandstone",b="Agmond's trail comes in from the west, and the blood smeared over stone and sand tells how far the dwarf crawled before dying here. Beside the lifeless hand, scratched into the Badlands sandstone, is a single word: Murdaloc. Agmond's killer is to be slain, along with a number of Stonevault Bonesnappers, and the news taken to Prospector Ironband in Loch Modan.",sp=0},{t="Ironband's Reply",b="Ironband takes the news soberly, remembering Agmond as strong of arm, fierce with a hammer and thick of skull. Ironband says Agmond was killed by cursed troggs, and is sure Agmond took a good number of them down along the way.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was Agmond?",a="Agmond was a dwarf in charge of the excavation sites in the Badlands for Prospector Ironband. Your search for Agmond ended at a skeleton.",al={"who is agmond","agmond lore"}},{q="Who is Murdaloc?",a="Murdaloc is the name scrawled in the sandstone beside Agmond's dead hand. You are to slay Agmond's killer, Murdaloc.",al={"what is murdaloc","murdaloc lore"}},{q="Where does the report need to go?",a="To Prospector Ironband in Loch Modan.",al={"who do i tell about murdaloc","where is ironband"}}},kw={"agmond","badlands","loch modan","murdaloc","prospector ironband","stonevault bonesnapper","trogg"},rel={"quest:738","npc:prospector-ironband","zone:badlands","zone:lochmodan","topic:trogg","topic:dwarf"},m={start="Battered Dwarven Skeleton",["end"]="Prospector Ironband",level="42",faction="Alliance",id=739},src={"Murdaloc (quest)"}}
E["quest:762"] = {t="quest",n="An Ambassador of Evil",z="badlands",s="Historian Karnik wants Ambassador Infernus of Angor Fortress put down. You are to go back into the Badlands, and carry proof of the kill to Advisor Belgrum in Ironforge.",h="Historian Karnik wants Ambassador Infernus of Angor Fortress put down.",sec={{t="The Ambassador in Angor Fortress",b="Ragnaros himself sent Ambassador Infernus to Angor Fortress to oversee the Shadowforge as they hunt for lost artifacts in Uldaman. The toll in dwarven lives has already been heavy and is worsening. Karnik dares not guess how many artifacts the Shadowforge might find and use against Ironforge. You are to go back to the Badlands, destroy Infernus, and bring Belgrum proof of your victory. Time presses, since Ragnaros will not wait for them to prepare.",sp=0},{t="Belgrum's Thanks",b="Belgrum praises your dedication to Ironforge and the dwarven people, and will send word of your success to Karnik. Help will also be sent to the Badlands to retake the excavation site. Belgrum has one thing more to ask of you, in King Bronzebeard's name.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Ambassador Infernus?",a="Ragnaros himself sent Infernus to Angor Fortress to oversee the Shadowforge as they hunt for lost artifacts in Uldaman.",al={"who is infernus","infernus lore","ambassador infernus background"}},{q="Where is Ambassador Infernus?",a="In Angor Fortress, in the Badlands.",al={"where to find ambassador infernus","ambassador infernus location","where is infernus"}},{q="Why does Karnik want Ambassador Infernus destroyed?",a="The Shadowforge's search in Uldaman has already cost many dwarven lives, and Karnik fears the artifacts they find could be used against Ironforge.",al={"why kill ambassador infernus","what is infernus doing in uldaman","ironforge threat badlands"}},{q="Who gives and ends this quest?",a="Historian Karnik in Ironforge gives it, and you bring proof of victory to Advisor Belgrum in Ironforge.",al={"who starts an ambassador of evil","who turns in ambassador of evil","ambassador of evil quest giver"}},{q="What proof is wanted?",a="Ambassador Infernus' Bracer, shown to Advisor Belgrum as proof of your victory.",al={"what do i need from infernus","ambassador infernus proof","infernus bracer"}}},kw={"advisor belgrum","ambassador infernus","angor fortress","badlands","historian karnik","ironforge","ragnaros","shadowforge","uldaman"},rel={"quest:725","zone:badlands","subzone:uldaman","zone:ironforge","quest:723","quest:720"},m={start="Historian Karnik",["end"]="Advisor Belgrum",level="44",faction="Alliance",id=762},src={"An Ambassador of Evil"}}
E["quest:777"] = {t="quest",n="This Is Going to Be Hard",z="badlands",s="Lucien Tosselwrench hands you cog #5 for Lotwil Veriatus, and heads for cover, inviting you to come along.",h="Lucien Tosselwrench hands you cog #5 for Lotwil Veriatus, and heads for cover, inviting you to come along.",sec={{t="Behind Cover",b="Lucien hands over the cog and says to take it to Lotwil Veriatus. Lucien will be waiting behind cover, and you are welcome to join. When you reach Lotwil, who is still bent over the shackles, a hand is held out and fingers waggle impatiently for the cog.",sp=0},{t="Making History",b="Lotwil takes the cog and says it is perfect, telling you to stand back while preparations are made to make more history. Lotwil carries on working feverishly.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who hands over the cog for Lotwil?",a="Lucien Tosselwrench gives you cog #5 to carry to Lotwil Veriatus.",al={"who gives the cog","where do i get cog 5","lucien cog"}},{q="Where does Lucien go?",a="Lucien goes behind cover and says you are welcome to join.",al={"why is lucien hiding","lucien cover"}},{q="What is Lotwil doing when you bring the cog?",a="Lotwil is working on a set of shackles and, without looking up, impatiently holds out a hand for the cog.",al={"what is lotwil doing","lotwil shackles","lotwil progress"}}},kw={"badlands","cog 5","lotwil veriatus","lucien tosselwrench","shackles","this is going to be hard"},rel={"quest:734","npc:lotwil-veriatus","zone:badlands"},m={start="Lucien Tosselwrench",["end"]="Lotwil Veriatus",level="42",faction="Neutral",id=777},src={"This Is Going to Be Hard (2)"}}
E["quest:778"] = {t="quest",n="This Is Going to Be Hard",z="badlands",s="Lotwil Veriatus declares the shackles finished and calls on Lucien, Servo and you to bear witness as a powerful elemental is summoned.",h="Lotwil Veriatus declares the shackles finished and calls on Lucien, Servo and you to bear witness as a...",sec={{t="A Groundbreaking Day",b="Lotwil cries out that the shackles are done and the time has come, calling Lucien and Servo to bear witness along with you. Lotwil presents the shackles as alchemy, engineering and the arcane in perfect combination, and means to summon a powerful elemental on what is declared a groundbreaking day for everyone there.",sp=0},{t="After the Summoning",b="The outcome is not what Lotwil expected, and Lotwil asks you to fetch the Shackles of Elemental Binding back after the Fam'retor Guardian is defeated. Afterwards, Lotwil is unsure what went wrong, but is glad that the magics were at hand to return the creature to the plane it came from.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Lotwil Veriatus?",a="Lotwil Veriatus is the maker of the Shackles of Elemental Binding, in which alchemy, engineering and the arcane are combined. Lucien and Servo are there with Lotwil in the Badlands.",al={"who is lotwil","lotwil veriatus"}},{q="What are the Shackles of Elemental Binding?",a="They are the shackles Lotwil has just finished, a combination of alchemy, engineering and the arcane, for use on a powerful elemental that Lotwil means to summon.",al={"what are the shackles","shackles of elemental binding"}},{q="Who does Lotwil call to bear witness?",a="Lotwil calls on Lucien and Servo to bear witness to the summoning, together with you.",al={"who is lucien","who is servo"}},{q="What comes before this step?",a="It follows the step in which you brought cog #5 to Lotwil.",al={"previous quest","what led to this"}}},kw={"badlands","elemental","fam'retor guardian","lotwil veriatus","lucien","servo","shackles of elemental binding"},rel={"npc:lotwil-veriatus","zone:badlands"},m={start="Lotwil Veriatus",["end"]="Lotwil Veriatus",level="45",id=778},src={"This Is Going to Be Hard (3)"}}
E["quest:782"] = {t="quest",n="Broken Alliances",z="badlands",s="In Kargath, Gorn wants the Horde's honor restored after its alliance with Deathwing. The ogre Boss Tho'grun, hired to help get the Sign of the Earth, turned on the Horde and kept it for himself, and you are to take it back at Camp Boff.",h="In Kargath, Gorn wants the Horde's honor restored after its alliance with Deathwing.",sec={{t="A Hired Band Turns",b="During the Second War the Horde stood with the dragon Deathwing. Blacklash and Hematus, a pair of his lieutenants, ended up locked away in Lethlor Ravine, far off to the east. Gorn holds that these depraved allies of old must be silenced if the Horde's honor is to be restored. To open the drakes' prison the Horde needed the Sign of the Earth, and hired ogre mercenaries under Boss Tho'grun to help find it. Tho'grun turned on them, overwhelmed them and kept it for himself.",sp=0},{t="Camp Boff",b="Gorn sends you southeast of Kargath to Camp Boff, to kill Tho'grun and carry the Sign of the Earth back. Gorn will be glad to see Tho'grun dead, and says the ogres are no longer part of the Horde.",sp=0},{t="What the Sign Opens",b="With Tho'grun dead, Gorn expects the ogres to fall into disarray, a small victory leading to a larger one. With the Sign in the Horde's hands, the black drakes' prison in Lethlor can be opened, freeing them from endless imprisonment, but to their doom.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Gorn?",a="Gorn is the Horde figure in Kargath who sends you after the Sign of the Earth, and wants to restore the Horde's honor by silencing its depraved allies of old.",al={"who gives broken alliances","gorn kargath","gorn lore"}},{q="Why does Gorn want Boss Tho'grun dead?",a="The Horde hired Tho'grun and his ogre mercenaries to help obtain the Sign of the Earth. Tho'grun turned on them, overwhelmed them and kept it.",al={"why kill thogrun","thogrun betrayal","boss thogrun lore"}},{q="Where is Camp Boff?",a="Camp Boff lies southeast of Kargath.",al={"camp boff location","where is thogrun","find boss thogrun"}},{q="What is the Sign of the Earth?",a="It is a key needed to unlock the prison of the drakes in Lethlor Ravine.",al={"sign of the earth","what does sign of the earth do"}},{q="Which dragons are imprisoned in Lethlor Ravine?",a="Blacklash and Hematus, two of Deathwing's lieutenants from the time of the Horde's alliance with him in the Second War.",al={"who is in lethlor ravine","blacklash and hematus","deathwing lieutenants"}}},kw={"badlands","blacklash","camp boff","deathwing","gorn","hematus","kargath","lethlor ravine","sign of the earth","tho'grun"},rel={"subzone:kargath","subzone:lethlor-ravine","npc:deathwing","topic:second-war","topic:horde","zone:badlands"},m={start="Gorn",["end"]="Gorn",level="43",faction="Horde",id=782},src={"Broken Alliances (1)"}}
E["quest:793"] = {t="quest",n="Broken Alliances",z="badlands",s="Gorn sends you to Lethlor Ravine in the far eastern Badlands, where the black drakes Blacklash and Hematus lie bound by the Seal of the Earth. This follows the first Broken Alliances.",h="Gorn sends you to Lethlor Ravine in the far eastern Badlands, where the black drakes Blacklash and Hematus...",sec={{t="Three Runestones",b="Three runestones keep the Seal of the Earth closed. Each rests in a pillar of Lethlor Ravine: Diamond, Opal and Amethyst. The Sign of the Earth, which Gorn gives you, draws the stones out and opens the seal. Countless drakes make their home in the ravine, and Blacklash and Hematus are formidable. Gorn wants both dead, and their bindings brought back.",sp=0},{t="What Gorn Makes of It",b="Gorn says the black dragonflight still stands allied with the renegade Blackrock orcs, and that dragons and orcs alike must be reined in or cast out. Once Blacklash and Hematus are dead, the Horde can look westward toward Blackrock Spire.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives this quest?",a="Gorn gives it, as the next step after the first Broken Alliances.",al={"broken alliances quest giver","gorn location","who gives broken alliances"}},{q="Where is Lethlor Ravine located?",a="Travel to the far eastern end of the Badlands. Countless drakes make their home in the ravine.",al={"lethlor ravine location","how to get to lethlor ravine","where is lethlor ravine"}},{q="How do you free Blacklash and Hematus?",a="The Sign of the Earth draws a runestone out of each of the three pillars. Set into the Seal of the Earth, those stones free both drakes.",al={"how to summon blacklash","seal of the earth","pillars of diamond opal amethyst"}},{q="What must be brought back to Gorn?",a="The bindings of Blacklash, the chains of Hematus and the Sign of the Earth, once both drakes are dead.",al={"broken alliances turn in items","what does gorn want back","bindings of blacklash"}}},kw={"black dragonflight","blacklash","blackrock orcs","gorn","hematus","lethlor ravine","seal of the earth","sign of the earth"},rel={"quest:782","subzone:lethlor-ravine","topic:black-dragonflight","zone:badlands"},m={start="Gorn",["end"]="Gorn",level="50",faction="Horde",id=793},src={"Broken Alliances (2)"}}
E["subzone:agmond-s-end"] = {t="subzone",n="Agmond's End",z="badlands",s="Agmond's End is an abandoned dwarven excavation site tucked into the southern hills of the Badlands. Once a hopeful exploratory dig led by the prospector Agmond, the camp turned into a slaughterhouse when burrowing troggs overran the operation and killed its leader.",h="Agmond's End is an abandoned dwarven excavation site tucked into the southern hills of the Badlands.",sec={{t="A Gruesome Excavation",b="Like many sites in the arid Badlands, Agmond's End began as a dwarven venture to uncover ancient relics and delve into the earth's buried history. That dream ended abruptly when savage troggs surged from the surrounding crevices and overwhelmed the miners. Agmond himself was cut down during the attack, giving the site its grim name. Today, the ruined dig remains utterly infested by Stonevault troggs, with shattered crates and abandoned tools left exactly where they fell.",sp=0},{t="A Lonely Neighbor",b="Near the ruined excavation sits a solitary camp inhabited by Theldurin the Lost, a dwarf whose sanity has long since frayed. He remains one of the few souls willing to brave the southern desert near the doomed site.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Agmond?",a="Agmond was a dwarven prospector who led an excavation into the southern Badlands. His survey ended in disaster when subterranean troggs emerged and butchered him and his expedition.",al={"who is agmond","agmond lore"}},{q="What creatures inhabit Agmond's End?",a="The ruined dig site is completely overrun by hostile troggs who slaughtered the dwarven miners and claimed the ruined camp and surrounding crags as their own.",al={"mobs at agmonds end","who lives here"}},{q="Who lives near Agmond's End?",a="A hermit dwarf known as Theldurin the Lost maintains a camp nearby in the southern hills, keeping a wary watch over the barren landscape.",al={"npc nearby","theldurin location"}},{q="Why were dwarves digging here in the first place?",a="Dwarven prospectors frequently survey the Badlands in search of titan artifacts, ancient ruins, and rich mineral seams, though many such expeditions underestimate the savage creatures lurking underground.",al={"why dwarven dig","purpose of excavation"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="The camp serves as a sobering reminder of the hazards of unearthing ancient earthen ground without sufficient martial support."},kw={"agmond","agmond's end","badlands","dig site","prospector","theldurin the lost","trogg"},rel={"zone:badlands","npc:theldurin-the-lost","topic:trogg"},src={"Agmond's End"}}
E["subzone:camp-kosh"] = {t="subzone",n="Camp Kosh",z="badlands",s="Camp Kosh is an ogre encampment in the northern Badlands, inhabited by the aggressive Dustbelcher ogres. Perched near vital travel routes, its brutes prey on passing caravans and scavenge whatever equipment travelers leave behind in the harsh desert.",h="Camp Kosh is an ogre encampment in the northern Badlands, inhabited by the aggressive Dustbelcher ogres.",sec={{t="A Den of Scavengers",b="Situated in the northern wastes of the Badlands, Camp Kosh serves as the northernmost settlement of the Dustbelcher ogres, who also occupy neighboring camps like Boff, Cagg, and Wurg. The ogres stationed here take advantage of their proximity to the roads, raiding vulnerable supply lines journeying toward Kargath or westward into the Searing Gorge. When dwarven prospectors led by Sigrun Ironhew were forced to flee the excavation at Uldaman, the brutes of Camp Kosh swiftly raided their abandoned wagons, hauling away precious food rations and armaments into the dusty encampment.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who lives in Camp Kosh?",a="Camp Kosh is inhabited by the Dustbelcher ogres, a tribe of brutal ogres that controls several small encampments across the arid Badlands.",al={"camp kosh mobs","who is at camp kosh","ogres camp kosh"}},{q="Why is Camp Kosh located here?",a="Its northern position allows the Dustbelcher ogres to ambushing supply caravans and unwary travelers moving between the Searing Gorge, Uldaman, and the Horde outpost of Kargath.",al={"why camp kosh","camp kosh location"}},{q="What did the ogres steal from the dwarves?",a="When Sigrun Ironhew's dwarven expedition retreated from the dangers inside Uldaman, they abandoned supply wagons in the desert. The ogres of Camp Kosh scavenged the wreckage, making off with crates of food and weapon shipments.",al={"dwarf supplies camp kosh","sigrun ironhew supplies","uldaman wagons"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="The scavenging ogres of Camp Kosh plundered the vital rations and weapon caches left behind by Sigrun Ironhew's beleaguered Uldaman expedition.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance scouts traveling the northern pass toward Searing Gorge must keep their guard up around Camp Kosh, as the brutes readily ambush passing supply caravans."},kw={"badlands","camp kosh","dustbelcher","ogres","sigrun ironhew","uldaman"},rel={"zone:badlands","subzone:uldaman","zone:searinggorge","subzone:kargath","topic:alliance"},src={"Camp Kosh"}}
E["subzone:camp-wurg"] = {t="subzone",n="Camp Wurg",z="badlands",s="Camp Wurg is an ogre encampment situated in the arid expanse of the Badlands. It serves as one of several outposts claimed by the territorial Dustbelcher ogres who dominate much of the Badlands.",h="Camp Wurg is an ogre encampment situated in the arid expanse of the Badlands.",sec={{t="A Dustbelcher Stronghold",b="Tucked among the crags of the Badlands, Camp Wurg is one of four primary camps settled by the Dustbelcher ogres, alongside Camp Cagg, Camp Boff, and Camp Kosh. The ogres stationed here guard their rugged territory fiercely, scavenging what they can from the unforgiving desert wastes. While rank-and-file brutes and enforcers dwell around the crude fires and rough hides of Wurg, their chieftain, Boss Tho'grun, maintains no permanent seat here, instead roaming the Badlands trails to keep watch over all his encampments.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who lives in Camp Wurg?",a="Camp Wurg is populated by the Dustbelcher ogres, a fierce and territorial tribe that has carved out settlements across the Badlands.",al={"camp wurg mobs","who is at camp wurg","who lives here"}},{q="Where is the leader of the camp?",a="The leader of the Dustbelcher ogres, Boss Tho'grun, does not stay confined to Camp Wurg. Instead, he patrols the open paths of the Badlands between Wurg, Cagg, Boff, and Kosh.",al={"camp wurg boss","boss thogrun location","who leads camp wurg"}},{q="What other camps belong to this tribe?",a="The Dustbelchers control four main strongholds throughout the Badlands: Camp Wurg, Camp Cagg, Camp Boff, and Camp Kosh.",al={"dustbelcher camps","other ogre camps badlands","ogre settlements badlands"}}},kw={"badlands","boss tho'grun","camp boff","camp cagg","camp kosh","camp wurg","dustbelcher","ogre","wurg"},rel={"zone:badlands"},src={"Camp Wurg"}}
E["subzone:crypt-badlands"] = {t="subzone",n="Crypt (Badlands)",z="badlands",s="Tucked away high in the dusty hills of the Badlands lies a secluded underground tomb known simply as the Crypt. Inside rests the silent remnant of an ancient warrior: an armored skeleton seated upon a stone throne, flanked by urns, chests, and a massive relic sword.",h="Tucked away high in the dusty hills of the Badlands lies a secluded underground tomb known simply as the...",sec={{t="The Tomb of the Barbarian King",b="Perched southeast of Hammertoe's Digsite along an unmarked earthen path rising up the hillside, the Badlands Crypt is easily missed by passersby. Down in its dark stone chambers sits an armored skeleton poised atop a throne. Resting beside the remains is the Sword of the Barbarian King, surrounded by scattered bones, urns, and forgotten chests. While miners and adventurers frequent the surrounding gullies in search of dwarven ruins and riches, the true origin and history of this seated sovereign remain a mystery lost to the arid wastes.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Crypt located in the Badlands?",a="The entrance is situated southeast of Hammertoe's Digsite. To reach it, follow an unmarked path winding up the crest of the hill above the digsite.",al={"badlands crypt location","how to find badlands crypt","crypt entrance badlands"}},{q="Who is the skeleton sitting on the throne inside?",a="The armored skeleton is commonly referred to as the Barbarian King. No surviving local texts detail his reign or identity, leaving him as an enigmatic relic of an earlier, forgotten era in the Badlands.",al={"skeleton on throne","who is the barbarian king","crypt skeleton identity"}},{q="What is the sword next to the throne?",a="It is known as the Sword of the Barbarian King. It rests silently beside the skeletal ruler, serving as a solemn grave marker and a testament to his warlike past.",al={"sword of the barbarian king","crypt sword","badlands throne sword"}},{q="Are there any quests associated with this crypt?",a="There are no standard quests directing adventurers into the crypt. It stands primarily as an eerie, hidden discovery for travelers scouring the cliffs.",al={"badlands crypt quest","why go to badlands crypt"}}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="The crypt offers warriors a moment of quiet reverence before a fallen champion who died clad in plate and still clutching his mighty blade.",["race:Dwarf"]="Though situated near active dwarven archaeological digsites, the architecture and skeletal throne point to mysteries predating Ironforge's recent excavations."},kw={"badlands","barbarian king","crypt","hammertoe's digsite","sword","throne"},rel={"zone:badlands"},src={"Crypt (Badlands)"}}
E["subzone:dustbowl"] = {t="subzone",n="Dustbowl",z="badlands",s="The Dustbowl is a sprawling, arid expanse in the northwestern Badlands, lying between the Horde outpost of Kargath and the central Valley of Fangs. Swept by scouring desert winds, it is a harsh wilderness populated by scavengers, prowling beasts, and wandering elementals. It is also the site of Camp Wurg, making it a frequent crossing point for travelers braving the wasteland.",h="The Dustbowl is a sprawling, arid expanse in the northwestern Badlands, lying between the Horde outpost of...",sec={{t="A Scorched Crossing",b="Stretching across the northwest of the Badlands, the Dustbowl is characterized by dry gulches, cracked clay, and relentless winds that stir up choking plumes of grit. Despite the barren landscape, tough desert flora persists in the form of hardy cacti and scattered, gnarled trees. The open flatland presents constant danger to unguided wayfarers, who must contend with predatory coyotes, circling buzzards, and living rock elementals born of the rugged earth. Tucked within this scrubland lies Camp Wurg, providing a recognizable landmark amidst the otherwise desolate expanse.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Dustbowl located?",a="The Dustbowl covers the northwestern region of the Badlands, situated directly between the fortified Horde encampment of Kargath to the west and the Valley of Fangs toward the center of the zone.",al={"dustbowl location","where is dustbowl","dustbowl badlands map"}},{q="What creatures wander the Dustbowl?",a="The area is prowled by fierce coyotes and circling buzzards looking for carrion. Travelers will also encounter dangerous rock elementals wandering the stony reaches.",al={"dustbowl mobs","what lives in dustbowl","dustbowl beasts"}},{q="What landmarks are found in the Dustbowl?",a="The most notable settlement within the Dustbowl is Camp Wurg, a visible waypoint amidst the arid desert between Kargath and the central plains.",al={"camps in dustbowl","camp wurg dustbowl"}},{q="Can any plant life survive out here?",a="Despite the dry and unforgiving climate, the Dustbowl hosts sparse vegetation, primarily hardy cacti and occasional withered desert trees adapted to the barren soil.",al={"dustbowl flora","plants in dustbowl"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Positioned just outside Kargath, the Dustbowl is the first open wilderness Horde scouts must cross when pushing eastward into the Badlands."},kw={"badlands","buzzards","camp wurg","coyotes","dustbowl","kargath","rock elementals","valley of fangs"},rel={"zone:badlands","subzone:camp-wurg","subzone:kargath","subzone:valley-of-fangs"},src={"Dustbowl"}}
E["subzone:kargath"] = {t="subzone",n="Kargath",z="badlands",s="Kargath is a fortified Horde outpost perched in the western Badlands, serving as their sole foothold in Khaz Modan. Established by the Kargath Expeditionary Force under Warchief Thrall's orders, the settlement anchors crucial transit lines across the Eastern Kingdoms while staging operations toward Blackrock Mountain and the excavation at Uldaman.",h="Kargath is a fortified Horde outpost perched in the western Badlands, serving as their sole foothold in Khaz...",sec={{t="A Bastion in Hostile Territory",b="Named in honor of the Shattered Hand chieftain Kargath Bladefist, the outpost of Kargath stands as the Horde's solitary settlement throughout the mountain realms of Khaz Modan. Surrounded by arid wastes, aggressive wildlife, and hostile dwarven factions, the garrison provides a vital midway sanctuary for travelers crossing the continent. Its flight master bridges the long divide between northern holdings like the Undercity and Hammerfall and southern redoubts like Stonard and Grom'gol Base Camp.",sp=0},{t="The Expeditionary Mission",b="Dispatched on direct orders from Warchief Thrall, the Kargath Expeditionary Force maintains a dual objective in the region. Troops make frequent forays into the ancient titan halls of Uldaman to uncover why Ironforge's Prospectors prize the dig site so dearly. Concurrently, scouts labor to carve a path through the Searing Gorge into Blackrock Mountain, seeking to strike at Rend Blackhand's false 'Dark Horde' while contending with the entrenched Dark Iron dwarves.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is this Horde town out in the middle of the Badlands?",a="Warchief Thrall ordered the Kargath Expeditionary Force to establish the outpost to secure regional footholds, probe the mysteries of the dwarven dig at Uldaman, and forge an invasion corridor into Blackrock Mountain against the Dark Horde.",al={"why is kargath here","purpose of kargath","who built kargath"}},{q="Who is Kargath named after?",a="The outpost is named after Kargath Bladefist, the famed chieftain of the Shattered Hand orc clan.",al={"kargath name origin","who was kargath","kargath bladefist outpost"}},{q="Why are the flight routes from Kargath so important?",a="Kargath serves as the vital logistical link connecting Horde outposts in northern Lordaeron, such as Undercity and Hammerfall, with their southern territories in Stranglethorn Vale and the Swamp of Sorrows.",al={"kargath flight path","why fly to kargath"}},{q="What threat is the garrison at Kargath preparing to fight?",a="The garrison regularly contends with local Dark Iron dwarves, investigates the Ironforge presence at Uldaman, and prepares an offensive against Rend Blackhand and his rival Dark Horde entrenched within Blackrock Mountain.",al={"kargath enemies","who does kargath fight"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Kargath is the Horde's only friendly fortress in all of Khaz Modan, offering essential resupply, flight connections, and launch points for strikes against Blackrock Mountain.",["race:Orc"]="Bearing the name of chieftain Kargath Bladefist, this outpost directly advances Thrall's campaign to eradicate Rend Blackhand's corrupted Dark Horde."},kw={"badlands","blackrock mountain","expeditionary force","kargath","kargath bladefist","shattered hand","thrall","uldaman"},rel={"zone:badlands","subzone:uldaman","subzone:blackrock-mountain","zone:searinggorge","npc:thrall","zone:undercity","subzone:hammerfall","subzone:stonard"},src={"Kargath"}}
E["subzone:lethlor-ravine"] = {t="subzone",n="Lethlor Ravine",z="badlands",s="Lethlor Ravine is a jagged, rocky canyon winding through the eastern reaches of the Badlands. It serves as a perilous roost and breeding ground for the black dragonflight, swarming with aggressive whelps and mature drakes.",h="Lethlor Ravine is a jagged, rocky canyon winding through the eastern reaches of the Badlands.",sec={{t="A Dragonflight's Bastion",b="Carved deep into the scorched plateaus of the eastern Badlands, Lethlor Ravine is one of the most hazardous stretches of the desert. The craggy canyon walls provide a natural aerie for the black dragonflight, housing nests of fierce dragon whelps guarded by larger, fire-breathing drakes. Few travelers dare approach the valley floor, as the shadows overhead constantly betray the flight of winged predators circling among the rocky spires.",sp=0},{t="Mysteries in the Dust",b="Beyond the scaly brood that claims it, Lethlor Ravine is marked by curious crystalline obelisks scattered throughout the crags. These crystalline formations are involved in a local quest chain. Their origin is not established.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Lethlor Ravine?",a="Lethlor Ravine is a deep, craggy canyon located on the eastern side of the Badlands, functioning primarily as a nesting ground for black dragons.",al={"where is lethlor ravine","what is this canyon","lethlor ravine info"}},{q="Why are there so many black dragons here?",a="The black dragonflight uses the sheltered, desolate rock formations of Lethlor Ravine to roost and rear their young, turning the canyon into a fortified nursery far away from major civilized cities.",al={"why are there dragons in badlands","lethlor dragons","black dragonflight in badlands"}},{q="What are the crystal obelisks in the ravine?",a="The crystalline obelisks are formations scattered throughout the ravine and involved in a local quest chain. Their origin is not established.",al={"lethlor crystal towers","pillars in lethlor ravine","obelisks badlands"}},{q="Is Lethlor Ravine safe for travelers?",a="No. The ravine is extremely dangerous, filled with flying drakes and aggressive whelps that attack trespassers on sight.",al={"can i walk through lethlor ravine","is lethlor ravine dangerous"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="The skies and ridges of Lethlor Ravine provide a stern test of marksmanship against fast-moving dragonkin and winged predators."},kw={"badlands","black dragonflight","drakes","lethlor ravine","obelisks","whelps"},rel={"zone:badlands","topic:black-dragonflight"},src={"Lethlor Ravine"}}
E["subzone:maker-s-terrace"] = {t="subzone",n="Maker's Terrace",z="badlands",s="The Maker's Terrace is a sprawling outdoor excavation site situated in the northern Badlands, directly fronting the entrance to the ancient titan vault of Uldaman. Travelers venturing south from Loch Modan must navigate its rugged perimeter, which is aggressively occupied by Dark Iron dwarves. The dig represents a contested threshold between the surface wastes and the titan mysteries entombed below.",h="The Maker's Terrace is a sprawling outdoor excavation site situated in the northern Badlands, directly...",sec={{t="Threshold of the Vault",b="Sprawling across the northern bluffs of the Badlands, the Maker's Terrace serves as the exterior staging ground for the subterranean halls of Uldaman. Long before travelers delve into the subterranean ruins, they must contend with the sun-scorched earthworks, scaffolding, and stone trenches of this grand excavation. It sits right along the pass coming down from Loch Modan, making it the first landmark greeting any traveler daring to venture into the arid wastes. The Terrace buzzes with violent industry as rival factions seek a way into the ancient secrets buried beneath the rock.",sp=0},{t="Dark Iron Occupation",b="The site is firmly under the boot of the Dark Iron clan, who patrol its ditches and perimeters with hostile vigilance. Drawn by the scent of titan relics and subterranean dominance, these subterranean dwarves dig incessantly into the hillside, seeking whatever armaments, records, or earthen relics the ancient Makers left behind. Anyone trying to reach the deep halls of Uldaman without clearing through these fortified sentries will quickly find themselves overwhelmed.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Maker's Terrace located?",a="The Maker's Terrace sits in the far north of the Badlands, right near the valley pass that connects the zone to Loch Modan. It surrounds the exterior entrance leading into the ancient complex of Uldaman.",al={"maker's terrace location","where is makers terrace","how to find makers terrace"}},{q="Who controls the Maker's Terrace?",a="The site is occupied and patrolled by hostile Dark Iron dwarves, who run active digging operations and fiercely guard the exterior approach to Uldaman against outsiders.",al={"who is at makers terrace","makers terrace enemies","who controls makers terrace"}},{q="What is the purpose of the excavation?",a="The Dark Iron dwarves are excavating the ancient titan complex of Uldaman. They seek to uncover relics, powerful machinery, and ancient titan secrets buried within the subterranean vaults before rival factions can claim them.",al={"why are they digging here","makers terrace dig","what are dark irons looking for"}},{q="Is Maker's Terrace part of Uldaman?",a="Yes, Maker's Terrace functions as the outer, open-air excavation pit that leads directly into the dungeon and caves of Uldaman.",al={"is this uldaman","makers terrace vs uldaman","terrace connection to dungeon"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves of Ironforge, seeing the Maker's Terrace in the hands of the treacherous Dark Iron clan is a bitter sight, as Uldaman holds the deepest secrets of dwarven origins.",["profession:Mining"]="The expansive quarries and earthworks carved into the sandstone cliffs show clear signs of heavy ore exploitation by dwarven excavators."},kw={"badlands","dark iron","excavation","maker's terrace","makers terrace","titans","uldaman"},rel={"subzone:uldaman","zone:badlands","zone:lochmodan"},src={"Maker's Terrace"}}
E["subzone:mirage-flats"] = {t="subzone",n="Mirage Flats",z="badlands",s="Mirage Flats is a barren, sun-scorched expanse nestled in the central wastes of the Badlands. Lying east of Dustbelch Grotto, this dry plateau is notorious for shimmering heat hazes and hungry predators.",h="Mirage Flats is a barren, sun-scorched expanse nestled in the central wastes of the Badlands.",sec={{t="A Scorched Wasteland",b="Situated east of Dustbelch Grotto, the Mirage Flats present travelers with an unforgiving stretch of cracked red dirt and shimmering heat waves that give the plain its name. Few civilized souls linger here; instead, the open flats are dominated by opportunistic scavengers and lethal beasts. Flocks of giant buzzards circle lazily on hot thermals above, watching for the leavings of ferocious ridge stalkers and pack-hunting crag coyotes that scour the brush for easy prey.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where are the Mirage Flats located?",a="The flats lie in the central Badlands, east of Dustbelch Grotto. Travelers passing between the western cliffs and the eastern canyons often find themselves crossing these sun-baked grounds.",al={"mirage flats location","where is mirage flats","mirage flats map"}},{q="Why is the area called Mirage Flats?",a="The name comes from the blinding desert sun and oppressive heat radiating off the flat, stony earth, creating persistent optical illusions and heat shimmers that can disorient parched travelers navigating the wastes.",al={"why called mirage flats","mirage flats name meaning","heat mirage badlands"}},{q="What creatures prowl the flats?",a="The area is populated by resilient predators and scavengers adapted to the harsh badlands. Pack-hunting rabid crag coyotes and prowling ridge stalker patriarchs hunt across the scrub, while giant buzzards circle overhead waiting to feast on whatever drops in the dust.",al={"mirage flats mobs","what lives in mirage flats","beasts of mirage flats"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="The wide, open plains of the Mirage Flats offer an abundance of aggressive beasts to track, study, or tame, particularly fierce ridge stalkers and resilient coyotes seasoned by desert survival."},kw={"badlands","crag coyote","dragon's mouth","dustbelch grotto","giant buzzard","mirage flats","ridge stalker"},rel={"zone:badlands","subzone:kargath"},src={"Mirage Flats"}}
E["subzone:uldaman"] = {t="subzone",n="Uldaman",z="badlands",s="Carved deep beneath the northern mountains of the Badlands, Uldaman is an ancient titan vault dating back to the ordering of the world. Recently unsealed by dwarven excavators, its halls contain the buried origins of the dwarven race alongside savage troggs and vigilant stone sentinels.",h="Carved deep beneath the northern mountains of the Badlands, Uldaman is an ancient titan vault dating back to...",sec={{t="The Vault of the First Creations",b="Uldaman was constructed by titan watchers as a subterranean redoubt and research facility. When early experiments in shaping living stone produced the misshapen troggs, the titans sealed their failed creations within the vault's stasis chambers and began anew, culminating in the stone-skinned earthen. Its deepest chambers came to hold vital archives, including the fabled Discs of Norgannon, guarded by the stonekeeper Archaedas and the giantess Ironaya. Dwarven legend holds that in time the stone-skinned earthen gave rise to the dwarven race, and that their cradle lay buried and forgotten beneath the hills.",sp=0},{t="Excavation and Turmoil",b="When Ironforge prospectors broke through Uldaman's exterior gates, their pickaxes inadvertently cracked open the stasis chambers. Hordes of awakened troggs overran the upper tunnels, driving back dwarven teams and severing early dig sites. Compounding the chaos, Dark Iron dwarves marched into the ruins seeking artifacts of supreme power for their fiery master, Ragnaros. Today, the deep shafts remain a war ground between rival dig teams, bloodthirsty troggs, and titan constructs that awaken to smash any trespasser regardless of clan or cause.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Uldaman?",a="Uldaman is a massive underground titan facility situated along the northern border of the Badlands. It was built in the world's dawn to quarantine failed titan experiments and house vast historical records, most notably the Discs of Norgannon.",al={"uldaman lore","what is this place","about uldaman"}},{q="Why is Uldaman important to the dwarves?",a="Dwarven legends suggest their ancestors, the stone-skinned earthen, were created within titan facilities like Uldaman. Finding and decoding the Discs of Norgannon buried at the heart of the ruins could unlock the definitive truth of dwarven origins.",al={"why do dwarves care about uldaman","dwarf origins","discs of norgannon"}},{q="Why are troggs infesting the ruins?",a="Troggs were the titans' first attempt at fashioning stone servants. When the experiment went awry, the titans locked them away in Uldaman's stasis vaults. Ironforge miners accidentally breached these pens, setting the troggs loose into the corridors and the surrounding mountains.",al={"where did troggs come from","why are troggs here","trogg origin"}},{q="What are the Dark Iron dwarves doing here?",a="Dark Iron incursions are searching for ancient titan artifacts, hoping to unearth powerful relics like the Discs of Norgannon to serve their elemental master, the Firelord Ragnaros.",al={"dark irons in uldaman","why are dark irons here"}},{q="Who guards the lowest chambers?",a="The deepest vault is protected by Archaedas, a massive stonekeeper who was tasked with safeguarding the complex and its knowledge alongside a legion of living stone constructs and golems.",al={"archaedas","who is the boss of uldaman","uldaman guardian"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Uldaman represents the threshold to your earliest heritage. For generations, the Ironforge clans wondered how they came to be; the answer lies engraved upon stone discs buried beneath these trogg-infested halls.",["profession:Mining"]="The titan-worked halls feature rich veins of rare earth and metals untouched for millennia, though extracting them means braving trogg ambushes and awakened stone sentinels."},kw={"archaedas","badlands","discs of norgannon","earthen","explorers league","ironaya","titan","trogg","uldaman"},rel={"zone:badlands","topic:titan","topic:explorers-league","topic:trogg","zone:ironforge","zone:lochmodan"},src={"Uldaman"}}
E["subzone:valley-of-fangs"] = {t="subzone",n="Valley of Fangs",z="badlands",s="The Valley of Fangs is a rugged, narrow pass carved between towering rock pillars in the central Badlands. Known for the vicious predators that prowl its dusty floor, it also shelters a small, isolated encampment of wandering tinkerers and exiles.",h="The Valley of Fangs is a rugged, narrow pass carved between towering rock pillars in the central Badlands.",sec={{t="A Treacherous Pass",b="Situated between two imposing stone formations in the heart of the Badlands, the Valley of Fangs earns its name from both the sharp silhouettes of its surrounding cliffs and the dangerous beasts roaming its floor. Feral crag coyotes, prowling cougars, and vicious wolves stalk the dusty corridor, making transit hazardous for lone travelers. Despite the hostile wildlife, a handful of wayward figures—including the banished orc Martek the Exiled and his goblin associates Rigglefuzz and Jazzrik—have pitched an informal camp here, tinkering away in seclusion far from the regional outposts.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Valley of Fangs located?",a="The Valley of Fangs lies in the central Badlands, tucked between two massive natural rock formations south of the main northern ridgeline.",al={"valley of fangs location","where is valley of fangs","valley of fangs map"}},{q="Who lives in the Valley of Fangs?",a="A small wayside camp can be found here, home to the lone orc Martek the Exiled and his tinkering goblin companions, Rigglefuzz and Jazzrik.",al={"who is in valley of fangs","valley of fangs camp","valley of fangs npcs"}},{q="Why is the valley dangerous to travel through?",a="The valley floor is heavily populated by aggressive wildlife native to the Badlands, notably predatory cougars, wolves, and coyotes that ambush wanderers in the narrow terrain.",al={"valley of fangs danger","valley of fangs mobs","what attacks you in valley of fangs"}},{q="Why did Martek and the goblins set up here?",a="Cast out and wandering the wastes, Martek the Exiled found a quiet, defensible niche between the rock walls alongside goblin associates willing to trade and tinker away from the prying eyes of major factions.",al={"why is martek here","why camp in valley of fangs","martek the exiled"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="The goblin tinkerers camped in the Valley of Fangs draw curious engineers seeking unconventional know-how in the middle of the arid wastes.",["class:Hunter"]="The dense population of tough cougars and wolves makes the valley a prime hunting ground for tracking quarry and taming rugged Badlands beasts."},kw={"badlands","cougars","jazzrik","martek the exiled","rigglefuzz","valley of fangs","wolves"},rel={"zone:badlands"},src={"Valley of Fangs"}}
E["zone:badlands"] = {t="zone",n="Badlands",z="badlands",s="The Badlands is an arid, sun-baked expanse of cracked earth, dust storms, and rocky canyons nestled between Loch Modan and Searing Gorge. Despite being deep within dwarven Khaz Modan, it serves as a volatile frontier dominated by Dark Iron dwarves, troggs, Dustbelcher ogres, and nesting black dragonkin. It also houses the titan ruins of Uldaman and the Horde stronghold of Kargath, making it a critical strategic waypoint.",h="The Badlands is an arid, sun-baked expanse of cracked earth, dust storms, and rocky canyons nestled between...",sec={{t="A Bleak Frontier",b="Wedged south of Loch Modan's verdant hills, the Badlands quickly turns into a sweltering basin of barren flats and rugged ravines. Surviving here requires contending with merciless coyotes, cougars, vultures, and fierce sandstorms that obscure the horizon. Scattered across the plateaus are the crude encampments of the Dustbelcher ogres, while the brooding Dark Iron clan fortifies Angor Fortress and clashes with anyone trespassing on their territory.",sp=0},{t="The Secrets of Uldaman",b="In the northern bluffs lies Uldaman, an ancient subterranean complex carved out by the titan-forged earthen. Recently uncovered by Ironforge prospectors, the excavation unearthed monumental secrets regarding the ancient ancestry of the dwarven race. However, digging into the subterranean vaults awoke hordes of vicious Stonevault troggs and animated earthen guardians, slaughtering archaeological teams and turning the digsites outside into bloody skirmish grounds.",sp=0},{t="The Shadows of Kargath and Lethlor",b="The Badlands is one of the Horde's most precarious footholds in the southern Eastern Kingdoms. Established in the northwest, the fortress of Kargath gives Warchief Thrall's forces a base of operations to keep watch on the rogue Dark Horde in nearby Blackrock Mountain. Meanwhile, to the far east lies Lethlor Ravine, a treacherous chasm where black whelps and dangerous black dragonkin guard their brooding grounds under the shadow of the mountains.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the Horde stationed in the Badlands?",a="The outpost of Kargath was established by the Kargath Expeditionary Force on orders from Warchief Thrall. Stationed under Warlord Goretooth, the encampment provides the Horde a vital staging ground to strike against Rend Blackhand and his renegade Blackrock clan entrenched within Blackrock Mountain.",al={"why kargath","horde in badlands","what is kargath"}},{q="How do you get to the Badlands?",a="Alliance travelers can walk directly south from Loch Modan through the Maker's Terrace pass. Horde travelers face a longer trek on foot through the southern hills of Loch Modan or through Searing Gorge via the western mountain pass before unlocking Kargath's flight master.",al={"getting to badlands","how to reach badlands","badlands entrance"}},{q="What is Uldaman?",a="Uldaman is a massive underground vault built by the ancient titans and their earthen servants. Though recently excavated by dwarven prospectors seeking the secrets of dwarven origins, the dig awoke buried earthen constructs and primitive Stonevault troggs, turning the ruin into a lethal battleground.",al={"what's uldaman","uldaman dungeon lore","who made uldaman"}},{q="What are the black dragons doing in Lethlor Ravine?",a="Lethlor Ravine serves as an eastern breeding and nesting canyon for the black dragonflight. Guarded by drakes and whelps, the clutch maintains a dangerous presence near the mountains, preying upon wanderers and guarding the eastern reaches from trespassers.",al={"dragons in badlands","lethlor ravine dragons","black dragonflight badlands"}},{q="Who controls Angor Fortress?",a="Angor Fortress is held by the hostile Dark Iron clan. Situated south of Uldaman, the fortress serves as a regional base where the Dark Irons conduct reconnaissance, contest the titan digsites, and battle neighboring ogres and surface explorers.",al={"angor fortress","badlands fortress","dark irons badlands"}},{q="Are there any friendly settlements for Alliance players here?",a="No. The Badlands has no fortified Alliance settlements or flight masters. Ironforge prospectors and solitary hermits maintain scattered, fragile camps near the digsites, but Alliance adventurers must rely on bases in Loch Modan or Searing Gorge for extensive supplies.",al={"alliance town badlands","alliance flight path badlands","friendly alliance badlands"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="The Badlands holds the answers to your very ancestry within Uldaman, where the discovery of the titan-forged earthen reshaped dwarven understanding of history.",["faction:Horde"]="Kargath serves as your sole military sanctuary deep in Khaz Modan, acting as the frontline against the Dark Horde occupying Blackrock Mountain.",["profession:Mining"]="The arid landscape is rich in iron, gold, truesilver, and mithril, including rare Indurium deposits found within Uldaman and the surrounding terrain."},kw={"angor fortress","badlands","dustbelcher","earthen","goretooth","kargath","lethlor","troggs","uldaman"},rel={"subzone:uldaman","subzone:kargath","zone:lochmodan","zone:searinggorge","subzone:lethlor-ravine","npc:warlord-goretooth","topic:dark-iron-clan","topic:black-dragonflight"},src={"Badlands (Classic)","Badlands"}}
